helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	sh	Determines the tangent of an angle. The angle is specified in radians.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	sh	Using the angle Alpha, the Tan Function calculates the ratio of the length of the side opposite the angle to the length of the side adjacent to the angle in a right-angled triangle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	sh	Tan(Alpha) = side opposite the angle/side adjacent to angle				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145174				0	sh	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	par_id3151042				0	sh	Tan (Number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080104.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156214				0	sh	Return value:				20181231 09:50:43
