helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	sh	Basic source code and dialogs are organized in a library system.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	sh	The LibraryContainer contains libraries				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	sh	Libraries can contain modules and dialogs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143271				0	sh	In Basic:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	par_id3153061				0	sh	The LibraryContainer is called \<emph\>BasicLibraries\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	sh	In dialogs:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	sh	The LibraryContainer is called \<emph\>DialogLibraries\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03131900.xhp	0	help	par_id3150543				0	sh	Both LibraryContainers exist in an application level and within every document. In the document Basic, the document's LibraryContainers are called automatically. If you want to call the global LibraryContainers from within a document, you must use the keyword \<emph\>GlobalScope\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
