helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415				0	sh	\<emph\>Text:\</emph\> Any valid string expression. Only the first character in the string is relevant.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	sh	Use the Asc function to replace keys with values. If the Asc function encounters a blank string, $[officename] Basic reports a run-time error. In addition to 7 bit ASCII characters (Codes 0-127), the ASCII function can also detect non-printable key codes in ASCII code. This function can also handle 16 bit unicode characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159413				0	sh	Example:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149457				0	sh	Sub ExampleASC				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150792				0	sh	Print ASC("A") REM returns 65				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	sh	Print ASC("Z") REM returns 90				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163800				0	sh	Print ASC("Las Vegas") REM returns 76, since only the first character is taken into account				20181231 09:50:43
