helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\07070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576	7			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_HELP_TEXT_SELECTION_MODE\"\>You can enable a selection cursor in a read-only text document or in the Help. Choose \<emph\>Edit - Select Text \</emph\>or open the context menu of a read-only document and choose \<emph\>Select Text\</emph\>. The selection cursor does not blink.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Run SQL command directly				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151100				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/14030000.xhp\" name=\"Run SQL command directly\"\>Run SQL command directly\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SbaNativeSql\"\>In Native SQL mode you can enter SQL commands that are not interpreted by $[officename], but are instead passed directly to the data source.\</ahelp\> If you do not display these changes in the design view, you cannot change back to the design view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149999				0	sh	For native SQL, the SQL string is forwarded directly to the connected database system without a previous evaluation by $[officename]. For example, if you access a database through an ODBC interface, the SQL string is passed to the ODBC driver and processed by it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3147226\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbanativesql.png\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3147226\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155893				0	sh	Run SQL command directly				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\14030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	sh	Click the icon again to return to normal mode, in which the changes in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"New Query Design\"\>New Query Design\</link\> are synchronized with the permitted changes through SQL.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Graphics Mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149762				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24020000.xhp\" name=\"Graphics Mode\"\>Graphics Mode\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150255				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:GrafMode\"\>Lists view attributes for the selected graphic object. The embedded or linked graphic object in the current file will not be changed, only the view of the object.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3154515\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.528in\" height=\"0.292in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154515\"\>Cell Styles\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	sh	Graphics mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155262				0	sh	Default				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434				0	sh	The view of the graphic object is not changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	sh	Grayscale				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153760				0	sh	The graphic object is shown in grayscale. A color graphic object can become monochrome in grayscale. You can also use the color sliders to apply a uniform color to the monochrome graphic object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151246				0	sh	Black and White				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153062				0	sh	The graphic object is shown in black and white. All brightness values below 50% will appear black, all over 50% will appear white.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146795				0	sh	Watermark				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\24020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	sh	The graphic object is raised in brightness and reduced in contrast so that it can be used in the background as a watermark. 				20181231 09:50:43
