helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToPattern\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a pattern field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148389				0	sh	Image Control				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3146927				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToImageControl\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into an image control.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149413				0	sh	Formatted Field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170001.xhp	0	help	par_id3083281				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ConvertToFormatted\" visibility=\"visible\"\>The selected control is transformed into a formatted field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Special properties of a formatted field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>formatted fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	sh	Special properties of a formatted field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	sh	\<emph\>Formatting\</emph\>: You can set the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>property by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button in the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> line of the \<emph\>Properties: Formatted Field\</emph\> dialog. The \<emph\>Number Format\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	sh	If the formatted field is connected to the text field of a database, the entries in this field will be treated as text. If the formatted field is connected to a field of the database that can be displayed as a number, the input is treated as numbers. The date and time are also handled internally as numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	sh	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	sh	\<emph\>Default value\</emph\>: This value is set for new records as the default value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>forms; data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; forms and subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>forms; subforms\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subforms; description\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"Data\"\>Data\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242	2			0	sh	The\<emph\> Data \</emph\>tab page defines the form properties that refer to the database that is linked to the form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	sh	Defines the data source on which the form is based, or specifies whether the data can be edited by the user. Apart from the sort and filter functions, you will also find all the necessary properties to create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154810				0	sh	Data source				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATASOURCE\"\>Defines the data source to which the form should refer.\</ahelp\> If you click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button, you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, where you can choose a data source.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146948				0	sh	Content				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCE\"\>Determines the content to be used for the form. The content can be an existing table or a query (previously created in the database), or it can be defined by an SQL-statement. Before you enter a content you have to define the exact type in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149657				0	sh	If you have selected either "Table" or "Query" in \<emph\>Content type\</emph\>, the box lists all the tables and queries set up in the selected database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148755				0	sh	Content type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CURSORSOURCETYPE\"\>Defines whether the data source is to be an existing database table or query, or if the form is to be generated based on an SQL statement.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	sh	If you choose "Table" or "Query", the form will refer to the table or query that you specify under \<emph\>Content\</emph\>. If you want to create a new query or a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, then you have to choose the "SQL" option. You can then enter the statement for the SQL query or the subform directly in the \<emph\>List content\</emph\> box on the Control properties Data tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158409				0	sh	Analyze SQL command				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ESCAPE_PROCESSING\"\>Specifies whether the SQL statement is to be analyzed by %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\> If set to Yes, you can click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button next to the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box. This will open a window where you can graphically create a database query. When you close that window, the SQL statement for the created query will be inserted in the \<emph\>Content\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	sh	Filter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FILTER_CRITERIA\"\>Enter the required conditions for filtering the data in the form. The filter specifications follow SQL rules without using the WHERE clause.\</ahelp\> For example, if you want to display all records with the "Mike" forename, type into the data field: Forename = 'Mike'. You can also combine conditions: Forename = 'Mike' OR Forename = 'Peter'. All records matching either of these two conditions will be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156212				0	sh	The filter function is available in user mode through the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12030000.xhp\" name=\"AutoFilter\"\>\<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\>\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090000.xhp\" name=\"Default Filter\"\>\<emph\>Default Filter\</emph\>\</link\> icons on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>\<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> Bar\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156005				0	sh	Sort				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SORT_CRITERIA\"\>Specifies the conditions to sort the data in the form. The specification of the sorting conditions follows SQL rules without the use of the ORDER BY clause.\</ahelp\> For example, if you want all records of a database to be sorted in one field in an ascending order and in another field in a descending order, enter Forename ASC, Name DESC (presuming Forename and Name are the names of the data fields).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156444				0	sh	The appropriate icons on the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Form Navigation Bar\"\>\<emph\>Form Navigation\</emph\> Bar\</link\> can be used in User mode to sort: \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12010000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Ascending\"\>\<emph\>Sort Ascending\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12020000.xhp\" name=\"Sort Descending\"\>\<emph\>Sort Descending\</emph\>\</link\>, \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12100100.xhp\" name=\"Sort\"\>\<emph\>Sort\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148616				0	sh	Add data only				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153139				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DATAENTRY\"\>Determines if the form only allows the addition of new data (Yes) or if it allows other properties as well (No).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	sh	If \<emph\>Add data only\</emph\> is set to "Yes", changing or deleting data is not possible.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148455				0	sh	Navigation bar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157976				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_NAVIGATION\"\>Specifies whether the navigation functions in the lower form bar can be used.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	sh	The "Parent Form" option is used for subforms. If you choose this option for a subform, you can navigate using the records of the main form if the cursor is placed in the subform. A subform is linked to the parent form by a 1:1 relationship, so navigation is always performed in the parent form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151051				0	sh	Cycle				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_CYCLE\"\>Determines how the navigation should be done using the tab key.\</ahelp\> Using the tab key, you can move forward in the form. If you simultaneously press the Shift key, the navigation will follow the opposite direction. If you reach the last (or the first) field and press the tab key again, it can have various effects. Define the key control with the following options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	sh	Option				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150424				0	sh	Meaning				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150417				0	sh	Default				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157847				0	sh	This setting automatically defines a cycle which follows an existing database link: If the form contains a database link, the Tab key will, by default, initiate a change to the next or previous record on exit from the last field (see All Records). If there is no database link the next/previous form is shown (see Current Page).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	sh	All records				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3152972				0	sh	This option applies to database forms only and is used to navigate through all records. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	sh	Active record				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3145301				0	sh	This option applies to database forms only, and is used to navigate within the current record. If you use the Tab key to exit from the last field of a form, the current record is changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3146913				0	sh	Current page				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3150330				0	sh	On exit from the last field of a form, the cursor skips to the first field in the next form. This is standard for HTML forms; therefore, this option is especially relevant for HTML forms.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155064				0	sh	Allow additions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_ADDITIONS\"\>Determines if data can be added.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156054				0	sh	Allow modifications				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156377				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_EDITS\"\> Determines if the data can be modified.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149019				0	sh	Allow deletions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148995				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_ALLOW_DELETIONS\"\>Determines if the data can be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153714				0	sh	Link master fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_MASTERFIELDS\"\>If you create a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170203.xhp\" name=\"subform\"\>subform\</link\>, enter the data field of the parent form responsible for the synchronization between parent and subform.\</ahelp\> To enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter after each input line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	sh	The subform is based on an \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#sql\" name=\"SQL\"\>SQL\</link\> query; more specifically, on a \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Parameter Query\"\>Parameter Query\</link\>. If a field name is entered in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box, the data contained in that field in the main form is read to a variable that you must enter in \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\>. In an appropriate SQL statement, this variable is compared to the table data that the subform refers to. Alternatively, you can enter the column name in the \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3156089				0	sh	Consider the following example:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151017				0	sh	The database table on which the form is based is, for example, a customer database ("Customer"), where every customer has been given a unique number in a data field named "Cust_ID". A customer's orders are maintained in another database table. You now want to see each customer's orders after entering them into the form. In order to do this you should create a subform. Under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\> enter the data field from the customer database which clearly identifies the customer, that is, Cust_ID. Under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> enter the name of a variable which is to accept the data of the field Cust_ID, for example, x.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3151248				0	sh	The subform should show the appropriate data from the orders table ("Orders") for each customer ID (Customer_ID -> x). This is only possible if each order is uniquely assigned to one customer in the orders table. Alternatively, you can use another field called Customer_ID; however, to make sure that this field is not confused with the same field from the main form, the field is called Customer_Number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153537				0	sh	Now compare the Customer_Number in the "Orders" table with the Customer_ID from the "Customers" table, which can be done, for example, using the x variable with the following SQL statement:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	sh	SELECT * FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform to show all data from the orders table)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3163727				0	sh	or:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	sh	SELECT Item FROM Orders WHERE Customer_Number =: x (if you want the subform from the orders table to show only the data contained in the "Item" field)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	sh	The SQL statement can either be entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, or you can create an appropriate parameter query, which can be used to create the subform.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150648				0	sh	Link slave fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3149923				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_SLAVEFIELDS\"\>If you create a subform, enter the variable where possible values from the parent form field can be stored.\</ahelp\> If a subform is based on a query, enter the variable that you defined in the query. If you create a form using an SQL statement entered in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> field, enter the variable you used in the statement. You can choose any variable name. If you want to enter multiple values, press Shift + Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	sh	If, for example, you specified the Customer_ID database field as a parent field under \<emph\>Link master fields\</emph\>, then you can define under \<emph\>Link slave fields\</emph\> the name of the variable in which the values of the Customer_ID database field are to be stored. If you now specify an SQL statement in the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> box using this variable, the relevant values are displayed in the subform.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152778				0	sh	What is a subform?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3155579				0	sh	Forms are created based on a database table or database query. They display the data in a visually pleasant fashion and can be used to enter data or edit data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3147094	34			0	sh	\<variable id=\"wozu\"\>If you require a form that can refer to the data in a table or query and can additionally display data from another table, you should create a subform. \</variable\> For example, this subform can be a text box that displays the data of another database table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3157972				0	sh	A subform is an additional component of the main form. The main form can be called the "parent form" or "master". Subforms are needed as soon as you want to access more than one table from a form. Each additional table requires its own subform.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id4807275				0	sh	After creating a form, it can be changed into a subform. To do this, enter Design Mode, and open the Form Navigator. In the Form Navigator, drag a form (that will become a subform) onto any other form (that will become a master).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	sh	The user of your document will not see that a form has subforms. The user only sees a document in which data is entered or where existing data is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2A				0	sh	Specify the Link master field from the data fields in the master form. In the subform, the Link slave field can be set as a field which will be matched to the contents of the Link master field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170203.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2D				0	sh	When the user navigates through the data, the form always displays the current data record. If there are subforms defined, the contents of the subforms will be displayed after a short delay of approximate 200 ms. This delay enables you to quickly browse through the data records of the master form. If you navigate to the next master data record within the delay limit, the subform data need not be retrieved and displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\stars.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Stars and Banners				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\stars.xhp	0	help	par_idN1055A				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/stars.xhp\"\>Stars and Banners\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\stars.xhp	0	help	par_idN1056A				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Stars and Banners toolbar from which you can insert graphics into your document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\stars.xhp	0	help	par_idN10594				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an icon on the Stars and Banners toolbar, and then drag in the document to draw the shape.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\stars.xhp	0	help	par_idN10597				0	sh	Some shapes have a special handle which you can drag to change the properties of the shape. The mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol over these special handles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151299				0	sh	Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156183				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>database contents; inserting as tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156183	18			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_AS_TABLE\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts data selected from the data source browser into the document as a table.\</ahelp\>In the \<emph\>Insert Database Columns\</emph\> dialog, select the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option to insert the selected data into the document as a table. In the dialog, you can decide which database fields or columns are transferred, and how the text table is formatted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152594				0	sh	Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152918				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> area, use the arrow keys to select the columns of the database table that you want to apply to the text table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156042				0	sh	Database columns				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152425	20			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TBL_DB_COLUMN\"\>Specifies the database columns to be inserted into the text table.\</ahelp\> All database table columns that have not been accepted in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box are listed here. The entries are sorted alphabetically. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147577				0	sh	Table column(s)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_TABLE_COL\"\>Lists all database columns to be inserted into the document.\</ahelp\> A column will be assigned to each corresponding entry in the table. The entry order in the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box determines the data order in the text table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146958				0	sh	>>				20181231 09:50:43
