helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Events				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>forms; events\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>events;in forms\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170202.xhp\" name=\"Events\"\>Events\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147043				0	sh	The\<emph\> Events \</emph\>tab page, allows you to assign a macro to certain events which occur in a form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	sh	To link an event with a macro, first write a macro that contains all the commands to be executed when the event happens. Then assign this macro to the respective event by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the corresponding event. The\<emph\> Assign Macro \</emph\>dialog opens, where you can select the macro.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	sh	The following actions can be configured individually, meaning that you can use your own dialogs to depict an action:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	sh	Displaying an error message,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	sh	Confirming a delete process (for data records),				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	sh	Querying parameters,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155261				0	sh	Checking input when saving a data record.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	sh	For example, you can issue a "confirm deletion" request such as "Really delete customer xyz?" when deleting a data record.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200920562590				0	sh	The events that are shown in the Events dialog cannot be edited directly. You can delete an event from the list by pressing the Del key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	sh	The following lists and describes all events in a form that can be linked to a macro:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	sh	Before update				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Before update event occurs before the control content changed by the user is written into the data source.\</ahelp\> The linked macro can, for example, prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153779				0	sh	After update				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_AFTERUPDATE\"\>The After update event occurs after the control content changed by the user has been written into the data source.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157909				0	sh	Prior to reset				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390	51			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVERESETTED\"\>The\<emph\> Prior to reset \</emph\>event occurs before a form is reset.\</ahelp\> The linked macro can, for example, prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	sh	A form is reset if one of the following conditions is met:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	sh	The user presses an (HTML) button that is defined as a reset button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	sh	A new and empty record is created in a form that is linked to a data source. For example, in the last record, the \<emph\>Next Record\</emph\> button may be pressed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156119				0	sh	After resetting				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148563	55			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RESETTED\"\>The\<emph\> After resetting \</emph\>event occurs after a form has been reset.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870				0	sh	Before submitting				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152	28			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_SUBMITTED\"\>The\<emph\> Before submitting \</emph\>event occurs before the form data is sent.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149167				0	sh	When loading				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423	6			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_LOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When loading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been loaded.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148451				0	sh	Before reloading				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154218	39			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RELOADING\"\>The\<emph\> Before reloading \</emph\>event occurs before the form is reloaded.\</ahelp\> The data content has not yet been refreshed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155102				0	sh	When reloading				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3157895	41			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_RELOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When reloading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been reloaded.\</ahelp\> The data content has already been refreshed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152792				0	sh	Before unloading				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598	43			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_UNLOADING\"\>The\<emph\> Before unloading \</emph\>event occurs before the form is unloaded; that is, separated from its data source.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154145				0	sh	When unloading				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154638	45			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_UNLOADED\"\>The\<emph\> When unloading \</emph\>event occurs directly after the form has been unloaded; that is, separated from its data source.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147426				0	sh	Confirm deletion				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154988	26			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_CONFIRMDELETE\"\>The\<emph\> Confirm deletion \</emph\>event occurs as soon as data has been deleted from the form.\</ahelp\> For example, the linked macro can request confirmation in a dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149481				0	sh	Before record action				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3156007	58			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEROWCHANGE\"\>The\<emph\> Before record action \</emph\>event occurs before the current record is changed.\</ahelp\> For example, the linked macro can request confirmation in a dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145749				0	sh	After record action				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975	59			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ROWCHANGE\"\>The\<emph\> After record action \</emph\>event occurs directly after the current record has been changed.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154012				0	sh	Before record change				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	60			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_POSITIONING\"\>The\<emph\> Before record change \</emph\>event occurs before the current record pointer is changed.\</ahelp\>. For example, the linked macro can prevent this action by returning "FALSE".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157975				0	sh	After record change				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098	61			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_POSITIONED\"\>The\<emph\> After record change \</emph\>event occurs directly after the current record pointer has been changed.\</ahelp\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151076				0	sh	Fill parameters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_APPROVEPARAMETER\"\>The\<emph\> Fill parameters \</emph\>event occurs when the form to be loaded has parameters that must be filled out.\</ahelp\> For example, the data source of the form can be the following SQL command:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148773				0	sh	SELECT * FROM address WHERE name=:name				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149581				0	sh	Here :name is a parameter that must be filled out when loading. The parameter is automatically filled out from the parent form if possible. If the parameter cannot be filled out, this event is called and a linked macro can fill out the parameter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146926				0	sh	Error occurred				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485	10			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_EVT_ERROROCCURED\"\>The\<emph\> Error occurred \</emph\>event is activated if an error occurs when accessing the data source.\</ahelp\> This applies to forms, list boxes and combo boxes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Form Controls				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154142				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>form controls;toolbars\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; form fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>form fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command button creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>push buttons;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>radio button creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>check box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>labels; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fixed text; form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text boxes;form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>list box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>picklist creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drop-down lists in form functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combo box creation\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; select mode\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154142				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Form Controls\"\>Form Controls\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151378				0	sh	\<variable id=\"formulartext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Config\"\>The Form Controls toolbar contains tools that you need to create an interactive form.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> You can use the toolbar to add controls to a form in a text, spreadsheet, presentation, or HTML document, for example a button that runs a macro.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id1027200809391346				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	sh	Icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar (you may need to enable this initially invisible icon):				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3150943\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_config.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150943\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	sh	Form Controls				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B21				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xforms.xhp\"\>XML Form documents\</link\> (XForms) use the same controls.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152771				0	sh	To create a form, open a document and use the Form Controls toolbar to add and define the form controls. If you want, you can also link the form to a database, so that you can use the controls to manipulate a database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	sh	When you create a form in an HTML document, you can use the form to send data over the Internet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	sh	%PRODUCTNAME only exports the form properties that are supported by the HTML version that you export to. To specify the HTML version, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C39				0	sh	To add a control to a document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	sh	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the icon of the control that you want to add.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C4D				0	sh	In the document, drag to create the control. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C50				0	sh	To create a square control field, hold down the Shift key while you drag.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127				0	sh	To add a field from the field list of a table or query to a form, drag a cell into the form. In a text document, you can also drag a column header to add a field to a form. To include a label for the field, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift key down when you drag a column head.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C87				0	sh	Modifying a Control				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	sh	Right-click the control and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>. A dialog opens where you can define the properties of the control.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	sh	To specify a accelerator key for a control, add a tilde (~) in front of the character in the label for the control.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152792	135			0	sh	You can drag and drop controls from one document to another document. You can also copy and paste controls between documents. When you insert a control from another document, $[officename] analyzes the data source, content type, and content properties of the control so that the control fits the logical structure in the target document. For example, a control that displays contents from an address book continues to display the same contents after you copy the control to a different document. You can view these properties on the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab page of the \<emph\>Form properties\</emph\> dialog. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154411				0	sh	Select				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3153516\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153516\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150470				0	sh	This icon switches the mouse pointer to the select mode, or deactivates this mode. The select mode is used to select the controls of the current form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146914				0	sh	Check Box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148483				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3156380\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_checkbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156380\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:CheckBox\"\>Creates a check box.\</ahelp\> Check boxes allow you to activate or deactivate a function in a form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	sh	Text Box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3153266\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_edit.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153266\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Edit\"\>Creates a text box.\</ahelp\> Text boxes are fields in which the user can enter text. In a form, text boxes display data or allow for new data input.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151218				0	sh	Formatted Field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154836				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3143277\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formattedfield.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143277\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147547				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FormattedField\"\>Creates a formatted field.\</ahelp\> A formatted field is a text box in which you can define how the inputs and outputs are formatted, and which limiting values apply.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155346				0	sh	A formatted field has \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170002.xhp\" name=\"special control properties\"\>special control properties\</link\> (choose \<emph\>Format - Control\</emph\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148774				0	sh	Push Button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3151073\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertpushbutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151073\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147046				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Pushbutton\"\>Creates a push button.\</ahelp\> This function can be used to execute a command for a defined event, such as a mouse click.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	sh	You can apply text and graphics to these buttons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157844				0	sh	Option Button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3152999\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_radiobutton.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152999\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RadioButton\"\>Creates an option button.\</ahelp\> Option buttons enable the user to choose one of several options. Option buttons with the same functionality are given the same name (\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170101.xhp\" name=\"Name\"\>\<emph\>Name\</emph\>\</link\>\<emph\>property\</emph\>). Normally, they are given a \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170000.xhp\" name=\"group box\"\>group box\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156064				0	sh	List Box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3154135\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_listbox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154135\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ListBox\"\>Creates a list box.\</ahelp\> A list box lets users select an entry from a list. If the form is linked to a database and the database connection is active, the\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"List Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>List Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after the list box is inserted in the document. This wizard helps you create the list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147171				0	sh	Combo Box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3148817\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_combobox.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148817\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149407				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ComboBox\"\>Creates a combo box.\</ahelp\> A combo box is a single-line list box with a drop-down list from which users choose an option. You can assign the "read-only" property to the combo box so that users cannot enter other entries than those found in the list. If the form is bound to a database and the database connection is active, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170900.xhp\" name=\"Combo Box Wizard\"\>\<emph\>Combo Box Wizard\</emph\>\</link\> will automatically appear after you insert the combo box in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145618				0	sh	Label Field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3151017\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfixedtext.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151017\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Label\"\>Creates a field for displaying text.\</ahelp\> These labels are only for displaying predefined text. Entries cannot be made in these fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	sh	More Controls				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CDC				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/more_controls.xhp\"\>\<emph\>More Controls\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
