helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3145357				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_EMPTY_IS_NULL\"\>Defines how an empty string input should be handled. If set to Yes, an input string of length zero will be treated as a value NULL. If set to No, any input will be treated as-is without any conversion.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200812403467				0	sh	An empty string is a string of length zero (""). Normally, a value NULL is not the same as an empty string. In general, a term NULL is used to denote an undefined value, an unknown value, or "no value has been entered yet."				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id0820200812403455				0	sh	Database systems vary and they might handle a value NULL differently. Refer to documentations of the database that you are using.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161653				0	sh	Filter proposal				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170102.xhp	0	help	par_id3151221	89			0	sh	\<variable id=\"filtervorschlag\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_FILTERPROPOSAL\"\>While designing your form, you can set the "Filter proposal" property for each text box in the \<emph\>Data\</emph\> tab of the corresponding \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog. In subsequent searches in the filter mode, you can select from all information contained in these fields.\</ahelp\> The field content can then be selected using the AutoComplete function. Note, however, that this function requires a greater amount of memory space and time, especially when used in large databases and should therefore be used sparingly. \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
