helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Conversion of measurement units				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147543				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>measurement units; converting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>units; converting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;metrics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>metrics;converting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147543				0	sh	Conversion of measurement units				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069F				0	sh	In some dialogs, you can enter measurement values into input boxes. If you just enter a numerical value, the default measurement unit is used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A2				0	sh	You define the default measurement unit for Writer text documents in the dialog that you get by choosing \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</emph\>. For Calc, Draw, and Impress, you open a document of that type and then open the appropriate \<emph\>General\</emph\> page as for Writer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AD				0	sh	In input boxes for length units you can also add the unit abbreviation according to the following list:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	sh	Unit abbreviation				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	sh	Explanation				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	sh	mm				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	sh	Millimeter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D4				0	sh	cm				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DA				0	sh	Centimeter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E1				0	sh	in or "				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	sh	Inch				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	sh	pi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106F4				0	sh	Pica				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FB				0	sh	pt				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10701				0	sh	Point				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10704				0	sh	The following formulas convert the units:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070A				0	sh	1 cm = 10 mm				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	sh	1 inch = 2.54 cm				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10712				0	sh	1 inch = 6 Pica = 72 Point				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	sh	For example, in a text document, open \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Indents & Spacing\</emph\>. To indent the current paragraph by one inch, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1 in\</item\> or \<item type=\"literal\"\>1"\</item\> into the "Before text" box. To indent the paragraph by 1 cm, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1 cm\</item\> into the input box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000003.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	sh	To input the maximum or minimum allowed value respectively, click the current value and then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Down\</item\> key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000407.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Window Menu				20181231 09:50:43
