helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000407.xhp	0	help	par_id3154545				0	sh	\<variable id=\"liste\"\>Choose \<emph\>Window\</emph\> - List of open documents\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Menu Commands				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156045				0	sh	Menu Commands				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	par_id3150838				0	sh	The window containing the document you want to work on must be selected in order to use the menu commands. Similarly, you must select an object in the document to use the menu commands associated with the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000011.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	sh	The menus are context sensitive. This means that those menu items are available that are relevant to the work currently being carried out. If the cursor is located in a text, then all of those menu items are available that are needed to edit the text. If you have selected graphics in a document, then you will see all of the menu items that can be used to edit graphics.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Frequently-Used Buttons				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152952				0	sh	Frequently-Used Buttons				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147617				0	sh	Cancel				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155913				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Clicking \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> closes a dialog without saving any changes made.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id2341685				0	sh	Finish				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id6909390				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Applies all changes and closes the wizard.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	sh	Toolbars				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149783				0	sh	By clicking the arrow next to some icons you open a toolbar. To move a toolbar, drag the title bar. As soon as you release the mouse button, the toolbar remains at the new position. Drag the title bar to another position, or drag to an edge of the window, where the toolbar will dock. Close a toolbar by clicking the Close Window icon. Make the toolbar visible again by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - (toolbar name)\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152414				0	sh	Spin button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id1094088				0	sh	In form controls, a spin button is a property of a numerical field, currency field, date field, or time field. If the property "Spin button" is enabled, the field shows a pair of symbols with arrows pointing to opposing directions, either vertically or horizontally.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id7493209				0	sh	In the Basic IDE, a spin button is the name used for the numerical field together with the two arrow symbols.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155599				0	sh	You can type a numerical value into the field next to the spin button, or select the value with the up-arrow or down-arrow symbols on the spin button. On the keyboard you can press the up arrow and down arrow keys to increase or reduce the value. You can press the Page Up and Page Down keys to set the maximum and minimum value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150264				0	sh	If the field next to the spin button defines numerical values, you can also define a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000003.xhp#metrik\" name=\"measurement unit\"\>measurement unit\</link\>, for example, 1 cm or 5 mm, 12 pt or 2".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154232				0	sh	Convert				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you click forward through the dialog, this button is called \<emph\>Next\</emph\>. On the last page the button has the name \<emph\>Convert\</emph\>. The conversion is then performed by clicking the button.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145129				0	sh	Context Menu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156553				0	sh	\<variable id=\"context\"\>To activate the context menu of an object, first click the object with the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>left\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> mouse button to select it, and then, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>while holding down the Ctrl key or the Command and Option keys, click the mouse button again\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\> click the right mouse button\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Some context menus can be called even if the object has not been selected. Context menus are found just about everywhere in $[officename].\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	sh	Delete				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements after confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147557				0	sh	Delete				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Deletes the selected element or elements without requiring confirmation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148620				0	sh	Metrics				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	sh	You can enter values in the input fields in different units of measurement. The default unit is inches. However, if you want a space of exactly 1cm, then type "1cm". Additional units are available according to the context, for example, 12 pt for a 12 point spacing. If the value of the new unit is unrealistic, the program uses a predefined maximum or minimum value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155535				0	sh	Close				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Closes the dialog and saves all changes.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	sh	Close				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Closes the dialog.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156113				0	sh	Apply				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Applies the modified or selected values without closing the dialog.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153760				0	sh	Shrink / Maximize				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087	48			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click the\<emph\> Shrink \</emph\>icon to reduce the dialog to the size of the input field. It is then easier to mark the required reference in the sheet. The icons then automatically convert to the \<emph\>Maximize\</emph\> icon. Click it to restore the dialog to its original size.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062				0	sh	The dialog is automatically minimized when you click into a sheet with the mouse. As soon as you release the mouse button, the dialog is restored and the reference range defined with the mouse is highlighted in the document by a blue frame.				20181231 09:50:43
