helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200912381174				0	sh	OpenOffice.org 3.2, StarOffice 9.2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id0514200811525591				0	sh	In current versions, you can select to save your documents using ODF 1.2 (default) or ODF 1.0/1.1 (for backward compatibility). Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Load/Save - General\</item\> and select the ODF format version.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E9				0	sh	If you want to exchange documents with users that still use OpenOffice.org 1 or StarOffice 7, save the document using the respectively named filter in the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3146907				0	sh	If you want to define another file format as the default, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\> to find alternative file formats for each $[officename] document type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	sh	XML file structure				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3149649				0	sh	Documents in OpenDocument file format are stored as compressed zip archives that contain XML files. To view these XML files, you can open the OpenDocument file with an unzip program. The following files and directories are contained within the OpenDocument files:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3153178				0	sh	The text content of the document is located in \<emph\>content.xml\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3154068				0	sh	By default, \<emph\>content.xml\</emph\> is stored without formatting elements like indentation or line breaks to minimize the time for saving and opening the document. On the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> tab page you can activate the use of indentations and line breaks by clearing the check box \<emph\>Size optimization for ODF format\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3145152				0	sh	The file \<emph\>meta.xml\</emph\> contains the meta information of the document, which you can enter under \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740	33			0	sh	If you save a document with a password, \<emph\>meta.xml\</emph\> will not be encrypted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	sh	The file \<emph\>settings.xml\</emph\> contains further information about the settings for this document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447	35			0	sh	In \<emph\>styles.xml,\</emph\> you find the styles applied to the document that can be seen in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3153353	36			0	sh	The \<emph\>meta-inf/manifest.xml\</emph\> file describes the structure of the XML file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	sh	Additional files and folders can be contained in the packed file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154299				0	sh	Definition of the XML formats				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_idN10AAD				0	sh	The schema for the OpenDocument formats can be found on the \<link href=\"http://www.oasis-open.org\"\>www.oasis-open.org\</link\> web site.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3149561				0	sh	The DTD (Document Type Description) files for the older formats can be found in the installation folder.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000021.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	sh	Note that the formats are subject to certain licenses. You can find notes on the licenses at the start of the DTD files. More detailed information can be found on the \<link href=\"https://www.openoffice.org\" name=\"Apache OpenOffice\"\>Apache OpenOffice\</link\> website.				20181231 09:50:43
