helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	sh	Using forms, you can define how to present the data. Open a text document or a spreadsheet and insert the controls such as push buttons and list boxes. In the properties dialogs of the controls, you can define what data the forms should display.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	sh	Creating a New Form With the Form Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	sh	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can create a new form using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01090000.xhp\"\>Form Wizard\</link\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	sh	Open the database file where you want to create the new form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	sh	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Forms\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_forms.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Form\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
