helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Changing Default Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154285				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>modifying, see changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing, see also editing and replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default templates; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating; templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates;editing and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resetting;templates\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154285				0	sh	\<variable id=\"standard_template\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/standard_template.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Templates\"\>Changing Default Templates\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	sh	When you open a new document with \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, a blank document appears based on a $[officename] template. You can edit, modify, or replace this template so that the new document contains your customized Styles or other contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	sh	Modifying Default Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	sh	First, open either an existing $[officename] template and modify it, or open a new document and edit it as necessary to create the desired template.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3159152				0	sh	You can define a document template for each $[officename] module. The following describes how to proceed for text documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145748	8			0	sh	Save the document by choosing\<emph\> File\</emph\> -\<emph\> Templates - Save \</emph\>and saving the document in the \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> category.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	sh	Double-click \<emph\>My Templates\</emph\> in the list on the left. You will see the user-defined templates in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\>. Select the template you have just saved and open the context menu or open the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146901				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Set As Default Template\</emph\>. The next time you open a new text document, the new document will be based on the new default template.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153947				0	sh	Resetting Default Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3156276				0	sh	To reset the modified text template to the original default template:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	sh	Open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reset default template\</emph\>. In the submenu, select the document type whose default setting you want to restore. Thereafter, when you open an empty text document, it will again correspond to the $[officename] default template for text documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153764				0	sh	Using Custom Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386	14			0	sh	There are several ways to make your work easier by using your own custom templates. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149109				0	sh	Templates in the Template Folder				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	sh	You can save a new template with \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\> or by selecting "Template" file type in any Save dialog. Save the template in the user directory specified under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Paths\</emph\> to be able to access the template from within the \<emph\>File - New - From Templates and Documents\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	sh	You may need to update the view of the templates in the dialog before you can see a newly created template. In this case, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\> and in the submenu of the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> button, choose \<emph\>Update\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	sh	To open the template for editing, choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\standard_template.xhp	0	help	par_id3147315				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110000.xhp\" name=\"Templates\"\>Templates\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
