helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digital_signatures.xhp	0	help	par_id3448591				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a document using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145071				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data source view; drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;from data source view\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	sh	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_beamer\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_beamer.xhp\" name=\"Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\"\>Drag-and-Drop With the Data Source View\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111				0	sh	A fast way of copying from a data source into a text or spreadsheet document, or of creating forms based on a data source, is by drag-and-drop.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3155390\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155390\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	sh	Copying with Drag-and-Drop				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	sh	If you want to reverse a drag-and-drop, position the cursor in your document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	sh	It is also possible to copy by drag-and-drop from a document into a data source:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	sh	A text table or the selected range of a spreadsheet can be dragged using drag-and-drop to a table container in the data source explorer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	sh	Plain text can be copied using drag-and-drop from one document to a data field in the data source view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421				0	sh	Using data in a text document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685				0	sh	You can insert a database field in a text document by dragging a field name from the column header of the data source view into the document. This is especially useful when designing form letters. Simply drag the desired fields - home address, form of address, and so on - into your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153105				0	sh	To insert a complete record, select the corresponding header and drag it into the document. When you release the mouse button, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert database columns\"\>\<emph\>Insert database columns\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can decide whether to use all database fields, and whether to copy the data into the document as text, a table or fields. All currently selected records will be inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	sh	Applying data to a table document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864				0	sh	You can insert one or more records into the current sheet of a spreadsheet by selecting the rows in the data source view and dragging and dropping them into the spreadsheet. The data is inserted at the place where you release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766				0	sh	Inserting controls in a text form				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	sh	When you create a text form linked to a database, you can generate controls by drag-and-drop from the data source view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	sh	When you drag a database column into the text document, you insert a field. If you hold down Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging, a text field is inserted, grouped with an appropriate label field. The text field already contains all the database information that you need for the form.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	bm_id7430951				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>opening;documents on WebDAV server\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>digital signatures;WebDAV over HTTPS\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	hd_id4989165				0	sh	\<variable id=\"digitalsign_receive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/digitalsign_receive.xhp\"\>Opening a Document Using WebDAV over HTTPS\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	sh	In %PRODUCTNAME, you can open and save documents that are stored on a WebDAV server, using the secure HTTPS protocol.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	sh	You must use the %PRODUCTNAME file dialogs to use WebDAV over HTTPS.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	sh	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - General\</item\>. Ensure that \<emph\>Use %PRODUCTNAME dialogs\</emph\> is enabled. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id7424237				0	sh	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter the path to the WebDAV folder. For example, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>https://192.168.1.1/webfolder\</item\> to open a secure connection to the WebDAV server at the IP address 192.168.1.1, and to list the contents of the \<item type=\"literal\"\>webfolder\</item\> folder.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	sh	The first time you connect to a WebDAV server, you see the "\<emph\>Website Certified by an Unknown Authority\</emph\>" dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	sh	You should click the \<emph\>Examine Certificate\</emph\> button and examine the certificate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	sh	If you accept the certificate, choose "\<emph\>Accept this certificate temporarily for this session\</emph\>" and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. Now you can open and save files from the WebDAV server without further questions, until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	sh	If you do not trust the certificate, click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	sh	If you did accept the certificate, you can now select the file name or file names you want to open and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	sh	If there is a mismatch of the domain name given in the certificate and the domain name you entered in the file dialog, then you see a dialog that allows you to choose from any of the following options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	sh	 \<emph\>View Certificate\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the View Certificate dialog.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	sh	 \<emph\>Continue\</emph\> - \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If you are sure both domains are the same, click the Continue button.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id9116794				0	sh	 \<emph\>Cancel Connection\</emph\> - Cancels the connection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	sh	If you click \<emph\>Continue\</emph\>, you may see a dialog that asks you to enter your user name and password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your user name to log on to the WebDAV server.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter your password.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\digitalsign_receive.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If you enable \<emph\>Remember password till end of session\</emph\>, your password will be remembered for subsequent WebDAV connections until you exit %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
