helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Registering an Address Book				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	sh	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	sh	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	sh	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	sh	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	sh	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	sh	Address Data Source Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	sh	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	sh	Registering An Existing Address Book Manually				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	sh	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Address Data Source ...\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	sh	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	sh	When finished, close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	sh	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	sh	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	sh	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	sh	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144547360				0	sh	In Writer text documents, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	sh	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	sh	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	sh	Select one of the options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	sh	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	sh	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	sh	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	sh	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	sh	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	sh	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	sh	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>databases; text formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables in text format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; spreadsheets to text format\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154824				0	sh	\<variable id=\"data_dbase2office\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_dbase2office.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	sh	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBASE import and export, you can use a common text format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	sh	Importing Data into $[officename]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	sh	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	sh	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	sh	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	sh	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	sh	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	sh	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBASE format in the folder of a dBASE database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBASE" and the folder of the dBASE database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	sh	Exporting in CSV Text Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	sh	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	sh	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	sh	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Creating Reports 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	bm_id3729667				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;reports\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	sh	\<variable id=\"data_reports\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_reports.xhp\"\>Creating Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	sh	A report is a Writer text document that can show your data in an organized order and formatting. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, you have a choice to create a report either manually using drag-and-drop in the Report Builder window, or semi-automatic by following a series of dialogs in the Report Wizard. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4094363				0	sh	The following list gives you some information to decide which method to use for your data:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8514358				0	sh	Report Builder				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9764091				0	sh	Report Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1579638				0	sh	Started by "Create Report in Design View" command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1886959				0	sh	Started by "Use Wizard to Create Report" command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id455030				0	sh	Full flexibility to use report headers and footers, page headers and footers, multi-column reports.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8409985				0	sh	Uses a Writer template to generate a report document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5931272				0	sh	Use drag-and-drop to position the record fields or other design elements like pictures or lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9869075				0	sh	Select from several given choices to arrange the data records.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8611713				0	sh	Generates a one-time snapshot of the data. To see an updated report, execute the same report again to create a Writer document with the updated data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2866908				0	sh	You can choose to generate a one-time snapshot with fixed data, or a "live" report with links to the current data at the time when you open the Base file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4169743				0	sh	Saves the report as a Writer text document. Stores the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id408948				0	sh	Saves the report and the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2891933				0	sh	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to create a new report with the current data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id6142765				0	sh	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to either see again the static snapshot of the data from first creation time, or to create a new report with the current data. This depends on your choice on the last page of the wizard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1757560				0	sh	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to open the Report Builder window, with the report's information loaded.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4649189				0	sh	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to edit the Writer template file that was used to create the report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	hd_id8414258				0	sh	Creating a New Report Manually In Design View				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id3119602				0	sh	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4226508				0	sh	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5758842				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Create Report in Design View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	sh	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> guide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	sh	Creating a New Report With the Report Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DC				0	sh	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E0				0	sh	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E8				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Report\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8032166				0	sh	Follow the steps of the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100000.xhp\"\>Report Wizard\</link\> to create the report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156410				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>start parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command line parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>parameters;command line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arguments in command line\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156410				0	sh	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009				0	sh	By starting the $[officename] software from the command line you can assign various parameters, with which you can influence the performance. The use of command line parameters is only recommended for experienced users.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	sh	For normal handling, the use of command line parameters is not necessary. A few of the parameters require a deeper knowledge of the technical background of the $[officename] software technology.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	sh	Starting the $[officename] Software From the Command Line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152				0	sh	Under Windows, select \<emph\>Run\</emph\> from the Windows Start menu, or open a Shell under UNIX® based platforms.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472	6			0	sh	Under Windows, type the following text in the \<emph\>Open \</emph\>text field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	sh	Under UNIX based systems, type the following line of text, then press \<emph\>Return\</emph\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147561	7			0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>{install}\\program\\soffice.exe {parameter} \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>{install}/program/soffice {parameter} \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	sh	Replace \<emph\>{install}\</emph\> with the path to your installation of the $[officename] software (for example, \<emph\>C:\\Program Files\\Office\</emph\>, or \<emph\>~/office\</emph\>)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	sh	Where required, replace \<emph\>{parameter}\</emph\> with one or more of the following command line parameters.				20181231 09:50:43
