helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Error Report Tool				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150616				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>reports;error reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>crash reports\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>activating;Error Report Tool\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150616				0	sh	\<variable id=\"error_report\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/error_report.xhp\" name=\"Error Report Tool\"\>Error Report Tool\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	sh	The Error Report Tool starts automatically when a program crash occurs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	sh	The Error Report Tool gathers all necessary information that can help the program developers to improve the code, so that in later versions this error can possibly be avoided. Please help us to improve the software and send the generated error report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148538				0	sh	Starting the Error Report Tool				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	sh	With most program crashes the Error Report Tool will start automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154046				0	sh	Completing the Report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	sh	On the main Error Report Tool dialog, you can enter some additional information that may help the developers to localize the error. For example, if the error only appears after a change in your hardware or software environment, or if you clicked on a button, please include that information.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159399				0	sh	Sending the Error Report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504				0	sh	The Error Report Tool uses the HTTP PUT / SOAP protocol to send the report data. You may optionally enter some descriptive text that will help us to identify the context of the program crash. Then click the \<emph\>Send\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670				0	sh	You will not get an answer to your error report. If you need support, please visit the \<link href=\"text/shared/main0108.xhp\"\>support forum\</link\> on the Internet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	sh	You may choose to respond to questions that the developers may have about the reported error. Mark the check box if you allow to be contacted by e-mail, should additional information be required. By default this box is not marked, so you will not get any e-mail.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	sh	What Data is Sent?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	sh	The error report consists of several files. The main file contains information about the error type, operating system name and version, memory usage, and the description that you entered. You can click the \<emph\>Show Report\</emph\> button on the main dialog of the Error Report Tool to view what will get sent in the main file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\error_report.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	sh	In addition, relevant memory contents and stack traces are gathered by some system standard tools ("dbhhelp.dll" on Windows systems, "pstack" on UNIX systems). This information will be sent also.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>protecting; contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protected contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>contents protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>encryption of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>passwords for protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>security;protecting contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>form controls; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>graphics;protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames;protecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	sh	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153394				0	sh	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	sh	Protecting All Documents When Saving				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150775				0	sh	All documents that are saved in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000021.xhp\" name=\"OpenDocument format\"\>OpenDocument format\</link\> can be saved with a password. Documents that are saved with a password cannot be opened without the password. The content is secured so that it cannot be read with an external editor. This applies to content, graphics and OLE objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	sh	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145121				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box. Save the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154286				0	sh	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	sh	Open the document, entering the correct password. Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145068				0	sh	Information entered in \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\> is not encrypted. This includes the name of the author, creation date, word and character counts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	sh	Protecting Revision Marking				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3161646				0	sh	With every change made in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer, the review function records who made the change. This function can be turned on with protection, so that it can only be turned off when the correct password is entered. Until then, all changes will continue to be recorded. Acceptance or rejection of changes is not possible.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	sh	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	sh	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. Enter the correct password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155113				0	sh	Protecting Frames, Graphics, and OLE Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153703				0	sh	You can protect the content, position and size of inserted graphics. The same applies to frames (in Writer) and OLE objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147131				0	sh	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	sh	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Contents\</emph\>, \<emph\>Position\</emph\> and/or \<emph\>Size\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147510				0	sh	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153657				0	sh	For example, for graphics inserted in Writer: Choose \<emph\>Format - Picture - Options\</emph\> tab. Under \<emph\>Protect\</emph\>, unmark as appropriate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152992				0	sh	Protecting Drawing Objects and Form Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166429	59			0	sh	The draw objects that you insert into your documents with the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar can be protected from being accidentally moved or changed in size. You can do the same with form objects inserted with the \<emph\>Form Controls\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153226				0	sh	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148815	61			0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Mark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3156289				0	sh	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154991	63			0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Object - Position and Size \</emph\>- \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\> tab. Unmark the \<emph\>Position\</emph\> or \<emph\>Size\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	sh	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4680928				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id9014252				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\"\>Protecting Cells in %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Switching Between Insert Mode and Overwrite Mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159233				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>text; overwriting or inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>overwrite mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>insert mode for entering text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159233				0	sh	\<variable id=\"textmode_change\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/textmode_change.xhp\" name=\"Switching Between Insert Mode and Overwrite Mode\"\>Switching Between Insert Mode and Overwrite Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	sh	With the keyboard:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031	3			0	sh	Press Insert to toggle between overwrite mode and insert mode. The current mode is displayed on the Status Bar.\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\> The text cursor must be enabled in the cell or in the input line. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152349				0	sh	With the mouse:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	sh	On the Status Bar, click on the area indicating the current mode in order to switch to the other mode:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3145673				0	sh	\<emph\>INSRT\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3154307	7			0	sh	Insert mode is enabled. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The text cursor is a blinking vertical line. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>Click on the area to enable the overwrite mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	sh	\<emph\>OVER\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491	9			0	sh	The overwrite mode is enabled. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>The text cursor is a blinking block. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>Click on the area to enable insert mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\textmode_change.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/04/01010000.xhp\" name=\"Keyboard commands\"\>Keyboard commands\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154136				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>graphics, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images, see also pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting and editing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>illustrations, see pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pixel graphics; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invert filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>smoothing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sharpening filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remove noise filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>solarization filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aging filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>posterizing filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pop-art filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charcoal sketches filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mosaic filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154136				0	sh	\<variable id=\"insert_bitmap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_bitmap.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\"\>Inserting, Editing, Saving Bitmaps\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	sh	Inserting Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	sh	A bitmap image can be inserted in $[officename] Writer, $[officename] Calc, $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149236				0	sh	Select the file. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box you can restrict the selection to certain file types.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153126				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box if you want a link to the original file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	sh	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is marked, whenever the document is updated and loaded the bitmap image is reloaded. The editing steps that you have carried out in the local copy of the image in the document are re-applied and the image is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	sh	If the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> box is not marked, you are always working with the copy created when the graphic was first inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	sh	To embed graphics that were first inserted as links, go to \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Break Link\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	sh	Editing Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id187078				0	sh	Icons on the Picture bar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	sh	When you select the bitmap image, the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar offers you the tools for editing the image. Only a local copy is edited in the document, even if you have inserted an image as a link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	sh	The \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar may look slightly different depending to the module you are using.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	13			0	sh	A number of filters are located on the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\" name=\"Graphic Filter\"\>Graphic \<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> toolbar, which you can open with the icon on the \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> Bar. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7055574				0	sh	The original picture file will not be changed by the filters. Filters are applied to a picture only inside the document. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	sh	Some of the filters open a dialog, which you can use to select, for example, the intensity of the filter. Most filters can be applied multiple times to increase the filter effect.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150105				0	sh	In $[officename] Draw and $[officename] Impress, you can add text and graphics, select these objects together with the bitmap, and export the selection as a new bitmap image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id2572405				0	sh	The Picture dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id6457411				0	sh	Right-click the picture and choose \<emph\>Picture\</emph\> from the submenu to open a properties dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id7991882				0	sh	Change the properties of the selected picture, then click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153574				0	sh	Saving Bitmaps				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	sh	If you want to save in a format such as GIF, JPEG or TIFF, you must select and export the bitmap image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803544667				0	sh	To export a bitmap in Draw or Impress:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	sh	Select the bitmap image. You can also select additional objects, such as text, to be exported with the image by pressing the shift key while selecting or by opening a selection frame around all objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Export\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3157139				0	sh	The \<emph\>Export\</emph\> command writes the picture with all applied filter effects to a file. The \<emph\>Save as Picture\</emph\> command in the context menu saves the picture without any filter effects, if the picture was inserted as a linked picture. An embedded picture will always be saved or exported with filters applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	sh	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> field, select the file format you want, for example GIF or JPEG.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3152462				0	sh	If you only want to export the selected objects, mark the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3150874				0	sh	If \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> is not marked, the entire page of the document is exported.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id3149417				0	sh	Enter a name for the file and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id0801200803525078				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>To export a bitmap in Writer: Right-click the bitmap, choose Save Graphics. You see the Graphics Export dialog. Enter a file name and select a file type.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_bitmap.xhp	0	help	par_id1033051				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/24010000.xhp\"\>Graphic Filter Bar from the Picture Bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>labels; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>business cards; creating and synchronizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>synchronizing;labels and business cards\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774				0	sh	\<variable id=\"labels\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/labels.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\"\>Creating and Printing Labels and Business Cards\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	sh	Designing Business Cards Through a Dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3146798	70			0	sh	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Business Cards\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Business Cards\</emph\>\</link\> to open the\<emph\> Business Cards \</emph\>dialog, which allows you to choose how your business cards will look.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147654				0	sh	Designing Labels and Business Cards				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	sh	You can design both labels and business cards through the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	sh	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010200.xhp\" name=\"File - New - Labels\"\>\<emph\>File - New - Labels\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Format\</emph\>, define the label format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	sh	$[officename] Writer contains many formats of commercially available sheets for labels, badges, and business cards. You can also add other, user-defined formats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Labels\</emph\> tab, under \<emph\>Inscription\</emph\>, you can choose what you want written on the labels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3145610				0	sh	This often involves database fields, so that the labels can be printed with varying content, when sending "Form Letters" for example. It is also possible to have the same text printed on every label.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	85			0	sh	Use the \<emph\>Database \</emph\>and \<emph\>Table \</emph\>list boxes to select the database and table from which the data fields are obtained. Click on the arrow button to transfer the selected data field into the inscription area. Press Enter to insert a line break. You can also enter spaces and any other fixed text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3147560				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> tab you can define your own label formats, not covered by the predefined formats. To do this, select "User" from the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list box. On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, you can specify whether all labels or only certain ones are to be created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150358				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, make sure that the \<emph\>Synchronize contents\</emph\> box is selected. If this is selected, a label only has to be entered (on the top left label) and edited once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	sh	As soon as you click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, you will see a small window with the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button. Enter the first label. When you click on the \<emph\>Synchronize Labels\</emph\> button, the current individual label is copied to all the other labels on the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3149767				0	sh	Click on \<emph\>New Document\</emph\> to create a new document with the settings you have entered.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\labels.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010300.xhp\" name=\"Business Cards\"\>Business Cards\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting and Editing Tab Stops				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144436				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;tab stops in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;tab stops\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;tab stops on ruler\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rulers; default settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rulers; measurement units\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>measurement units; changing on rulers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144436				0	sh	\<variable id=\"tabs\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/tabs.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\"\>Inserting and Editing Tab Stops\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id1376079				0	sh	On the horizontal ruler you can see the tab stops for the current paragraph. If you want to change the tab stops, you should first consider the scope to which you want to change tab stops as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id9434492				0	sh	Change the default tab stops for all documents: Use the menu \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id274971				0	sh	Change the tab stops for all paragraphs using the current Paragraph Style: Right-click the paragraph to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id5199133				0	sh	Change the tab stops for one or more paragraphs: Select the paragraphs, then click inside the ruler.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id6178167				0	sh	In the following, you find instructions for all above mentioned tasks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	27			0	sh	You can set a tab stop by clicking on the ruler or by selecting \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Tabs.\</emph\> Both methods affect the current paragraph or all selected paragraphs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	sh	Click the ruler once to set a left-justified tab. Right-click a tab icon on the ruler to see the context menu in which you can change the tab type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561				0	sh	To set several decimal tabs one after the other, keep clicking the icon to the left of the ruler until the desired tab type is shown, then click on the ruler.				20181231 09:50:43
