helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3153091				0	sh	Setting centered tabs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154150				0	sh	Double-click the ruler to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030300.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3154145				0	sh	Double-click the white area of the ruler to set one tab. The \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\> dialog appears with the \<emph\>Tabs\</emph\> tab page open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	sh	Moving Tabs on the Ruler				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145264				0	sh	Move individual tab stops on the ruler using the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	sh	To move several tab stops on the ruler, press the Shift key before you click a tab. Drag one tab while continuing to press Shift to move that tab as well as all the tabs to the right of it. The spacing between those tabs remains the same.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3147349	23			0	sh	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you drag a tab on the ruler to move that tab and all the tabs to the right of it. This results in the spacing between those tabs changing proportionally to their distance from the margin.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146146				0	sh	Changing the Properties of Tabs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3145646				0	sh	To change tab type, click the tab you want to change on the ruler, then right-click to open the context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154729				0	sh	Deleting Tabs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148879				0	sh	To delete a tab, hold down the mouse button while you drag the tab outside the ruler.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151074				0	sh	Changing the Defaults				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3151059				0	sh	If you want to change the settings of your default tab stops, you will find further information under \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Drawing - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Draw - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01070500.xhp\" name=\"Presentation - General\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>(module name) - General\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> in the Options dialog box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	sh	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\> of the ruler allows you to change the displayed units of measurement. These changes are only valid until you exit $[officename], and they only apply to the ruler on whose context menu you made the change. If you want to change the ruler measurement units permanently, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - [Document type] - View\</emph\> and change the measurement unit there.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\tabs.xhp	0	help	par_id3148429				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/main0213.xhp\" name=\"Ruler\"\>Ruler\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Integrating new UNO components				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149760				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>add-ons, see UNO components\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>UNO components;integrating new\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;UNO components\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149760				0	sh	\<variable id=\"integratinguno\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/integratinguno.xhp\" name=\"Integrating new UNO components\"\>Integrating new UNO components\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	sh	Programmers can write and integrate their own UNO (Universal Network Objects) components to $[officename]. Those new components can be added to the $[officename] menus and toolbars; we call them "Add-Ons".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	sh	The integration of new components is supported by some tools and services. Details can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide. The three main steps are as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	3			0	sh	Register the new components within $[officename]. This can be accomplished using the tool \<item type=\"literal\"\>unopkg\</item\>, which can be found in {installpath}\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>/ \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\\\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>program.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	sh	Integrate the new components as services. The ProtocolHandler and JobDispatch services assist you; more information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	sh	Change the user interface (menus or toolbars). This can be done almost automatically by writing an XML text file that describes the changes. More information can be found in the $[officename] Developer's Guide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\integratinguno.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	sh	The Add-Ons can extend the functionality of $[officename]. They are not related to the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Add-Ins\"\>Add-Ins\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Add-Ins\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> that provide new functions for $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Showing, Docking and Hiding Windows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150713				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery; hiding/showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data source view; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Navigator; docking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Styles and Formatting window; docking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; hiding/showing/docking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>docking; windows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>undocking windows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;docked windows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;docked windows\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145346				0	sh	\<variable id=\"autohide\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/autohide.xhp\" name=\"Showing, Docking and Hiding Windows\"\>Showing, Docking and Hiding Windows\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	sh	Some windows in $[officename] are dockable, such as the Navigator window. You can move these windows, re-size them or dock them to an edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154750				0	sh	Docking and Undocking Windows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	sh	To dock a window, do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	sh	Drag the window by its title bar to the side, or				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	sh	Double-click inside a vacant area of the window while holding down the Ctrl key. In the Styles and Formatting window, double-click a gray part of the window next to the icons while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. Alternatively, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F10\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	sh	These methods can also be used to undock a currently docked window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149796				0	sh	Showing and Hiding Docked Windows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3149655\" src=\"res/helpimg/ein.png\" width=\"0.1043inch\" height=\"0.4272inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149655\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\autohide.xhp	0	help	par_id3152921	64			0	sh	Click the button on the edge of the docked window to show or hide the docked window. The AutoHide function allows you to temporarily show a hidden window by clicking on its edge. When you click in the document, the docked window hides again. 				20181231 09:50:43
