helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2307199				0	sh	You can combine several graphic objects into a group so that you can use them like a single object. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9983825				0	sh	You can move, transform, resize, distort, or convert all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group any time to change the individual objects. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	sh	You can change the properties (line size, fill color, and more) of all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group and change the individual objects. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	sh	Groups can also be nested to form groups within other groups. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7705618				0	sh	To group objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id607013				0	sh	Select the objects together that you want to group. Hold down Shift while you click the individual objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	sh	Right-click any of the selected objects to open the context menu. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	sh	In Impress or Draw, choose Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group – Group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6738792				0	sh	To select the objects, you can also drag a selection frame around the objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	sh	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	sh	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7424237				0	sh	To enter a group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1388592				0	sh	Right-click any object of the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id343943				0	sh	In Impress or Draw, choose Enter Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Edit Group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8726767				0	sh	Now you can select and edit a single object in the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id691549				0	sh	You can add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	sh	The objects that are not part of the group are shown with dimmed colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id9141819				0	sh	To exit a group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	sh	Right-click any object of the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	sh	In Impress or Draw, choose Exit Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Exit Group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	sh	To exit a group in Draw or Impress, you can also double-click anywhere outside the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7889950				0	sh	To ungroup a group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3236182				0	sh	Right-click any object of the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1251258				0	sh	In Impress or Draw, choose Ungroup. In Calc or Writer, choose Group - Ungroup.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id8111819				0	sh	Now you can select and edit all objects as individual objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	sh	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	sh	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	sh	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	sh	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	sh	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	sh	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Languages Using Complex Text Layout				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153662				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>CTL;complex text layout languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>languages;complex text layout\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;CTL languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text layout for special languages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>right-to-left text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text from right to left\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bi-directional writing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hindi;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Hebrew;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Arabic;entering text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Thai;entering text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153662				0	sh	\<variable id=\"ctl\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ctl.xhp\" name=\"Languages Using Complex Text Layout\"\>Languages Using Complex Text Layout\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	sh	Currently, $[officename] supports Hindi, Thai, Hebrew, and Arabic as \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#ctl\" name=\"CTL languages\"\>CTL languages\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3155420				0	sh	If you select the text flow from right to left, embedded Western text still runs from left to right. The cursor responds to the arrow keys in that Right Arrow moves it "to the text end" and Left Arrow "to the text start".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145609				0	sh	You can change the text writing direction directly be pressing one of the following keys:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+D or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Right Shift Key - switch to right-to-left text entry				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149047				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+A or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Left Shift Key - switch to left-to-right text entry				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	sh	The modifier-only key combinations only work when CTL support is enabled.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3150541				0	sh	In multicolumn pages, sections or frames that are formatted with text flow from right to left, the first column is the right column and the last column is the left column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	sh	In $[officename] Writer text formatted in \<emph\>Thai language\</emph\> has the following features:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	sh	In paragraphs with justified alignment, the characters are stretched to flush the lines at the margins. In other languages the spaces between words are stretched.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909				0	sh	Use the Delete key to delete a whole composite character. Use the Backspace key to delete the last part of the previous composite character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3149809				0	sh	Use the Right or Left Arrow key to jump to the next or previous whole composite character. To position the cursor into a composite character, use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>Language Settings - Languages\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ctl.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01150300.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\"\>Language Settings - Complex Text Layout\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Selecting the Document Language				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id3083278				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>languages; selecting for text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters; language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>character styles;language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; language selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph styles; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drawings; languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults;languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; default languages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dictionaries, see also languages\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083278				0	sh	\<variable id=\"language_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Document Language\"\>Selecting the Document Language\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150040				0	sh	The language you select for your document determines the dictionary used for spellcheck, thesaurus and hyphenation, the decimal and thousands delimiter used and the default currency format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3153093				0	sh	The language you select applies to the whole document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	sh	Within the document, you can apply a separate language to any paragraph style. This has priority over the language of the whole document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	sh	You can assign a language to selected pieces of text in a paragraph, either by direct formatting or with a character style. This assignment has priority over the paragraph style and document language.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	sh	Selecting a language for the whole document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</emph\>. Go to \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Languages\"\>\<emph\>Language Settings - Languages\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	sh	Under \<emph\>Default languages for documents\</emph\>, select the document language for all newly created documents. If you mark \<emph\>For the current document only\</emph\>, your choice will only apply to the current document. Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152938				0	sh	Selecting a language for a Paragraph Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	sh	Place the cursor in the paragraph whose paragraph style you want to edit.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367				0	sh	Open the context menu and select \<emph\>Edit Paragraph Style\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	sh	All paragraphs formatted with the current paragraph style will have the selected language.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145801				0	sh	Applying a language directly to selected text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	sh	Select the text to which you want to apply a language.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3159348				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164				0	sh	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and proceed accordingly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	sh	Selecting a language for a Character Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	sh	Open the Styles and Formatting window and click on the \<emph\>Character Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3146792				0	sh	Click on the name of the character style to which you want to apply a different language.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150753				0	sh	Then open the context menu in the Styles and Formatting window and select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Character Style\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3150321				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3154756				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	sh	Now you can apply the character style to your selected text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id8703268				0	sh	Adding More Text Languages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7919248				0	sh	Dictionaries are supplied and installed as extensions. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Language - More Dictionaries Online\</item\> to open the dictionaries page in your default web browser.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id5174108				0	sh	Select a dictionary in the list of descriptions. Click the heading in a dictionary description that you want to get.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2897427				0	sh	In the next page, click the Get It icon to download the dictionary extension. Note the folder name to which your browser downloads the file. Download additional dictionaries as you like.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3906979				0	sh	In %PRODUCTNAME, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Extension Manager\</item\> and click Add to install the downloaded extensions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id0220200911174493				0	sh	After you installed the extensions, you should close %PRODUCTNAME (including the Quickstarter), and restart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9100924				0	sh	Setting UI Language				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2761314				0	sh	A standard installation of %PRODUCTNAME software will give you a user interface (UI) of your chosen language.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3912778				0	sh	Most users download the American English version, which gives you English menu commands and English application help. If you want another language for the menus (and for the application help, if available in that language), change the UI language as follows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id121158				0	sh	Select another UI language in the "User interface" listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3806878				0	sh	Click OK and restart the %PRODUCTNAME software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id130619				0	sh	If the listbox doesn't list the language that you want, see "Adding More UI Languages".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	hd_id9999694				0	sh	Adding More UI Languages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	sh	Open your Web browser and enter \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\"\>https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Download_OpenOffice.org_LanguagePacks\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	sh	Select and download the correct language pack for your version of %PRODUCTNAME software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	sh	Close %PRODUCTNAME software (also close the Quickstarter, if you enabled it).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\language_select.xhp	0	help	par_id3791924				0	sh	Install the language pack. Either double-click the exe file, or unpack the tar.gz file according to standard practice on your platform.				20181231 09:50:43
