helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	sh	\<variable id=\"import_ms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/import_ms.xhp\" name=\"Opening documents saved in other formats\"\>Opening documents saved in other formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	sh	You can open a document saved in another format by using the following procedure:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	5			0	sh	Select a format from the\<emph\> Files of type\</emph\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	sh	Select a file name and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	sh	If you always want the file dialogs to show another format by default, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - General\</emph\> and select that format as \<emph\>Default file format\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	sh	Converting all documents of a folder				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	sh	Open the wizard, which guides you through the operation, to copy and convert all documents from Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel or Microsoft PowerPoint into OpenDocument file format documents. You can select a source and target directory, specify whether to convert documents and/or templates, and more besides.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	sh	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id4563127				0	sh	Opening HTML files in Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id9207434				0	sh	Choose the file type "HTML Document" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web. This is the default for HTML documents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id7215491				0	sh	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web are now available to you, such as \<emph\>Show HTML source\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id2299874				0	sh	Choose "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id1727347				0	sh	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer are now available to you. Not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer offers for editing of documents can be saved in HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130100.xhp\" name=\"Working with VBA code\"\>Working with VBA code\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Setting the default file format\"\>Setting the default file format\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158421				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility;general shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys; %PRODUCTNAME accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158421				0	sh	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	sh	You can control \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> without using a mouse device, using only the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	sh	On each module's main help page (for example, the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer or \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main help page) there is a link to access the keyboard shortcuts' help for that module.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	sh	In addition, under the keyword "Accessibility" you find step-by-step instructions about how to control the selected module without a mouse device.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166460				0	sh	Working with the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> user interface without mouse				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154749				0	sh	Activating menu bar, toolbars, windows, and document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	sh	Repeatedly pressing F6 switches the focus and circles through the following objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	sh	menu bar,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	sh	every toolbar from top to bottom and from left to right,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	sh	every free window from left to right,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	sh	document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	sh	Press Shift+F6 to switch through objects in the opposite direction.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152473				0	sh	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to switch to the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	sh	Press F10 to switch to the menu bar and back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	sh	Escape closes an open submenu, a toolbar, or the current free window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161656				0	sh	Calling a menu command				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	sh	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> or F6 or F10 to select the first menu (the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu). With right arrow, the next menu to the right is selected; with left arrow, the previous menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	sh	Arrow down opens a selected menu. Any additional arrow down and up arrow move the selection through the menu commands. With right arrow you open any existing submenus.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	sh	Press Enter to execute the selected menu command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	sh	Executing an icon command				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	sh	Press F6 repeatedly until the first icon on the toolbar is selected. Use the right and left arrows to select an icon on a horizontal toolbar. Similarly, use the up and down arrows to select an icon on a vertical toolbar. The Home key selects the first icon on a toolbar and the End key, the last.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3144433				0	sh	Press Enter to execute the selected icon. If the selected icon normally demands a consecutive mouse action, such as inserting a rectangle, then pressing the Enter key is not sufficient: in these cases press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	sh	Pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on an icon for creating a draw object. A draw object will be placed into the middle of the view, with a predefined size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	sh	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter on the Selection tool to select the first draw object in the document. If you want to edit, size, or move the selected draw object, first use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to set the focus into the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	sh	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	sh	Special hints for toolbars				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	sh	Press the down arrow or right arrow to open the selected toolbar. This is equivalent to a mouse click. In the toolbar use the right arrow and left arrow keys. The Home and End keys select the first and last icon in the toolbar, respectively.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365				0	sh	Close the toolbar with Esc. It is not possible to move the toolbar without a mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	sh	Selection from a combo box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3148645\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.528in\" height=\"0.292in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148645\"\>Combo box\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	sh	Select the combo box. Press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	sh	Use the down arrow or Page Down key to scroll down the combo box entries, or the up arrow or Page Up key to scroll upwards. The Home key takes you to the first entry and the End key takes you to the last entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	sh	Press Enter to execute the selected entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685				0	sh	Selection in Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	sh	In several windows, dialogs, and in the table control field, there are tables to select data, for instance, in the right part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\" name=\"Data Source View\"\>Data Source View\</link\>. The following keys are used for selections in these tables:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	sh	Spacebar: switches from selection of the current row and cancellation of any selection, but not if the current cell is in edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar: switches between selection of the current row and cancellation of this selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149488				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+spacebar: switches between selection of the current column and cancellation of this selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Up Arrow or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Down Arrow: moves the window separator between table and form, for instance in the bibliography database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	sh	In a table control or in the data source view, the Tab key moves to the next column. To move to the next control, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab. To move to the previous control, press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592				0	sh	Size and Position of Windows and Dialogs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	sh	First press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+spacebar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	sh	A system menu opens with menu commands like \<emph\>Move\</emph\>, \<emph\>Resize\</emph\> and \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	sh	Choose a command (down arrow, then Enter).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155083				0	sh	Now you can use the arrow keys to move or resize the dialog or window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	sh	Press Enter to accept the change. Press Escape to cancel the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988				0	sh	Docking and Undocking Windows and Toolbars				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	sh	Press F6 until the window or toolbar is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	sh	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F10.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479				0	sh	Selecting objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993				0	sh	Press Shift+F4 to select the first object in the current document. When an object is selected, press Tab to select the next object, or press Esc to go back to the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152962				0	sh	Edit Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156379				0	sh	A selected OLE object can be activated with the Enter key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	sh	Edit Position and Size of Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	sh	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145619				0	sh	Set the grid resolution unit with \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> area. If you enter a number greater than 1 in the \<emph\>Subdivision\</emph\> area, you must press the arrow key as often as the number states to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	sh	Use the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	sh	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to enter the handle edit mode. The upper left handle is the active handle, it starts blinking. Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to select the next handle. Press Escape to exit the handle edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	sh	In the handle edit mode, the arrow keys move the selected handle, which changes the object size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	sh	Edit the Anchors of Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	sh	You can move the anchor of an object with the arrow keys. First enter the handle edit mode and select the anchor. Depending on the type of anchor, you can then move the anchor in different directions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	sh	Select the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646				0	sh	Enter the handle edit mode with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	sh	The upper left handle starts blinking. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab several times, until no handle blinks. This signals that now the anchor of the object is activated. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents you can press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A to activate the anchor directly.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	sh	Use the arrow keys to move the anchor. The object follows the anchor as appropriate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	sh	You can change the anchor of the selected object for example in the object's context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148393				0	sh	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To Paragraph\</emph\>, the arrow keys move the object to the previous or next paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615	69			0	sh	If the object is anchored\<emph\> To page\</emph\>, the keys Page Up or Page Down move it to the previous or next page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	sh	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To character\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it through the current paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256	71			0	sh	If the object is anchored\<emph\> As character\</emph\>, no anchor icon exists. You cannot move the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149527				0	sh	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To frame\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it to the next frame in the respective direction.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270				0	sh	Controlling the Dividing Lines				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413	134			0	sh	Documents of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw, and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress can be split horizontally and vertically into separate views. Each view can show other parts of the document. Using the mouse, you can drag a dividing line from the scrollbar into the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	sh	Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6: shows the dividing lines at default positions and focus a line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	sh	Arrow keys: moves the current dividing line a big step in the arrow direction.				20181231 09:50:43
