helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E0				0	sh	To insert a line break in a spreadsheet cell, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E3				0	sh	This will work only with the text edit cursor inside the cell, not at the input line. So first double-click the cell, then single-click at the text position where you want the line break.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\breaking_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914160968				0	sh	You can search for a newline character in the Find & Replace dialog by searching for \\n as a regular expression. You can use the text function CHAR(10) to insert a newline character into a text formula.				20181231 09:50:43
