helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150499				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>marking changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes; review function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function; recording changes example\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Track Changes, see review function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150499				0	sh	\<variable id=\"redlining\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining.xhp\" name=\"Recording and Displaying Changes\"\>Recording and Displaying Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id4013794				0	sh	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	sh	When several authors are working on the same text or spreadsheet, the review function records and displays who made the various changes. On the final edit of the document, it is then possible to look at each individual change and decide whether it should be accepted or rejected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	sh	For example: You are an editor and are delivering your latest report. But before publication the report must be read by the senior editor and the proofreader, and both will add their changes. The senior editor writes "clarify" after one paragraph and crosses out another entirely. The proofreader corrects the spelling of your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	sh	The edited document comes back to you, and you can incorporate or ignore the suggestions of the two reviewers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	sh	Let's say you also e-mailed a copy of the report to a good friend and colleague who has done research on a similar topic in the past. You asked for a few suggestions, and the document is now returned by e-mail with your colleague's suggestions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	sh	As all your colleagues and the managers in your company work with $[officename], you can produce a final version of the document from the results you get back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Collaboration				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	bm_id4459669				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>sharing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>collaboration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>file locking with collaboration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>locked documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id130008				0	sh	\<variable id=\"collab\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/collab.xhp\"\>Collaboration\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5821710				0	sh	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, Impress, and Draw, only one user at a time can open any document for writing. In Calc, many users can open the same spreadsheet for writing at the same time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9590136				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Share Document dialog where you can enable or disable collaborative sharing of the document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2519913				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enable to share the current document with other users. Disable to use the document unshared. This will invalidate the not yet saved edits that other users applied in the time since you last opened or saved this document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id6917020				0	sh	Collaboration in Calc				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4411145				0	sh	In %PRODUCTNAME Calc, document sharing allows simultaneous write access for many users. Every user who wants to collaborate should enter a name on the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6799218				0	sh	Some commands are not available (grayed out) when change tracking or document sharing is activated. For a new spreadsheet you cannot apply or insert the grayed out elements. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id3274941				0	sh	Creating a new spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9804681				0	sh	User A creates a new spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2109744				0	sh	The user does not want to share the spreadsheet for collaboration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5374614				0	sh	User A opens, edits, and saves the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id768761				0	sh	The user wants to share the document for collaboration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6844691				0	sh	The user chooses \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> to activate the collaboration features for this document. A dialog opens where the user can choose to enable or disable sharing. If the user enables sharing, the document will be saved in shared mode, which is also shown on the title bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5288857				0	sh	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Share Document\</item\> command can be used to switch the mode for the current document from unshared mode to shared mode. If you want to use a shared document in unshared mode, you would save the shared document using another name or path. This creates a copy of the spreadsheet that is not shared.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id8842127				0	sh	Opening a spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7276528				0	sh	User A opens a spreadsheet document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id8363902				0	sh	The spreadsheet document is not in shared mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	sh	The user can open, edit, and save the document as described above for Writer, Impress, and Draw documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5323343				0	sh	The spreadsheet document is in shared mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5824457				0	sh	The user sees a message that the document is in shared mode and that some features are not available in this mode. The user can disable this message for the future. After clicking OK, the document is opened in shared mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5800653				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If the same contents are changed by different users, the Resolve Conflicts dialog opens. For each conflict, decide which changes to keep.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6263924				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps your change, voids the other change.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id3609118				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the change of the other user, voids your change.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7184057				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps all your changes, voids all other changes.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id786767				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Keeps the changes of all other users, voids your changes.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2934965				0	sh	Saving a shared spreadsheet document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1174657				0	sh	User A saves a shared document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2577593				0	sh	The document was not modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id5883968				0	sh	The document is saved.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9049653				0	sh	The document was modified and saved by another user since user A opened the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id1976683				0	sh	If the changes do not conflict, the document is saved.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id43946				0	sh	If the changes conflict, the Resolve Conflicts dialog will be shown. User A must decide for the conflicts which version to keep, "Keep Mine" or "Keep Other". When all conflicts are resolved, the document is saved. While user A resolves the conflicts, no other user is able to save the shared document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id6449171				0	sh	Another user tries to save the shared document and resolves conflicts in this moment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7101046				0	sh	User A sees a message that a merge-in is in progress. User A can choose to cancel the save command for now, or retry saving some time later.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7186498				0	sh	When a user successfully saves a shared spreadsheet, the document will be reloaded after the save command, so that the spreadsheet shows the latest version of all changes that got saved by all users. A message shows that "foreign changes have been added" when another user did change some contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id2871791				0	sh	Collaboration in Writer, Impress, and Draw				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2675862				0	sh	For all modules Writer, Impress, Draw, and for Calc when document sharing is not enabled, a file locking is possible. This file locking is available even when accessing the same document from different operating systems:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7333597				0	sh	User A opens a document. The following conditions can apply:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id9976195				0	sh	The document is not locked by any other user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id2507400				0	sh	This document will be opened for read and write access by user A. The document will be locked for other users until user A closes the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id216681				0	sh	The document is marked as "read-only" by the file system.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id7709585				0	sh	This document will be opened in read-only mode. Editing is not allowed. User A can save the document using another document name or another path. User A can edit this copy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id4309518				0	sh	The document is locked by another user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id206610				0	sh	User A sees a dialog that tells the user the document is locked. The dialog offers to open the document in read-only mode, or to open a copy for editing, or to cancel the Open command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	hd_id29349651				0	sh	User access permissions and sharing documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id11746571				0	sh	Some conditions must be met on operating systems with a user permission management.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id25775931				0	sh	The shared file needs to reside in a location which is accessible by all collaborators.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id90496531				0	sh	The file permissions for both the document and the corresponding lock file need to be set so that all collaborators can create, delete, and change the files.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\collab.xhp	0	help	par_id71864981				0	sh	Write access also enables other users to (accidentally or deliberately) delete or change a file.				20181231 09:50:43
