helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id1413922				0	sh	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	sh	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	sh	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	sh	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"https://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>https://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	sh	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	sh	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	sh	To Create an XML Filter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	sh	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	sh	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	sh	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	sh	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	sh	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	sh	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	sh	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	sh	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	sh	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	sh	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DocType\</emph\> box, enter the document type identifier for the external file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0E				0	sh	This identifier is used to detect the file type on import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2C				0	sh	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DTD\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the DTD for the external file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D1F				0	sh	This DTD is used to validate the files on export.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A32				0	sh	In the \<emph\>XSLT for export\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from OpenDocument format to the external format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A38				0	sh	In the \<emph\>XSLT for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name to the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from the external format to OpenDocument format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	sh	(Optional) In the \<emph\>Template for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and name of the template that defines the %PRODUCTNAME styles that are used in the imported file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A44				0	sh	The files that are specified on the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page are copied to the local %PRODUCTNAME users directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A4C				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	sh	To Test an XML Filter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A5A				0	sh	You can perform basic tests on a custom XML filter in %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A91				0	sh	The document is not altered by these tests. 				20181231 09:50:43
