helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	sh	\<variable id=\"round_corner\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/round_corner.xhp\" name=\"Creating Round Corners\"\>Creating Round Corners\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	sh	When you insert a rectangle or a callout box using the drawing functions and activate the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, you see a small frame at the upper left corner of the object. The frame indicates the amount by which the corners are rounded. When the frame is positioned at the top left corner, no rounding occurs. When the frame is positioned on the handle centered at the top of the object, the corners are rounded as much as possible. You adjust the degree of rounding by moving the frame between these two positions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3150774\" src=\"res/helpimg/hand01.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150774\"\>Mouse pointer as hand\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	sh	If you place the cursor on the box it changes to a hand symbol. You can now drag the box to change the amount of rounding. An outline shows a preview of the result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; Internet Explorer for displaying $[officename] documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;viewing and editing in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	sh	\<variable id=\"activex\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/activex.xhp\" name=\"ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\"\>ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	sh	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346				0	sh	Installing the ActiveX control				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	sh	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	sh	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	sh	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	sh	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	sh	In the Installation Wizard, select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	sh	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry and find the \<emph\>ActiveX Control\</emph\> entry. Open the sub menu of the icon and select to install the feature.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	sh	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and \<emph\>Install\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	sh	Viewing $[officename] documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	sh	In Internet Explorer, browse to a web page that contains a link to a $[officename] Writer document, for example.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	sh	Click the link to view the document in the Internet Explorer window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154072				0	sh	You may still right-click the link to save the file on your harddisk.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	sh	Editing $[officename] documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367				0	sh	The $[officename] document inside the Internet Explorer shows a set of read-only toolbar icons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Edit file\</emph\> icon in the document's toolbar to open a copy of the document in a new $[officename] window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	sh	Edit the copy of the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	sh	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	sh	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	sh	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	sh	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	sh	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	sh	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	sh	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	sh	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	sh	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	sh	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	sh	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	sh	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	sh	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				20181231 09:50:43
