helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	sh	In the Help window, you can show or hide the navigation pane as needed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3156411				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3153345\" src=\"sfx2/res/indexon_small.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153345\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	sh	On the toolbar of the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> window, click the left icon to show or hide the navigation pane.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Editing Hyperlinks				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; editing hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;editing hyperlink buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;changing hyperlink URLs\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	sh	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Hyperlinks\"\>Editing Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id4124881				0	sh	When you \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click a hyperlink in a Writer document, your web browser opens with the requested web address. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the hyperlink and open the context menu by Shift+F10, then choose Open Hyperlink.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	sh	Change the text of a hyperlink as follows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	12			0	sh	In Writer documents, you can click anywhere into a hyperlink and edit the visible text. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id2690511				0	sh	If you leave the hyperlink by positioning the cursor somewhere else, only the visible text will be changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id1983092				0	sh	If you leave the hyperlink by entering a space character directly following the last character, the AutoCorrect - if enabled - will change the target URL to be the same as the visible text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id333262				0	sh	In all document types, you can open the Hyperlink dialog to edit a hyperlink. First set the cursor into the hyperlink or directly in front of the hyperlink, then click the Hyperlink icon on the Standard bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158432				0	sh	Change the URL of a hyperlink as follows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	sh	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	sh	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686				0	sh	Change the attribute of all hyperlinks				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	sh	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	sh	Click the Character Styles icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	sh	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	sh	In the dialog, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	sh	Edit a hyperlink button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	sh	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting Hyperlinks				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	sh	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	sh	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	sh	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	sh	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	sh	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	sh	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	sh	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	sh	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	sh	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	sh	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	sh	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
