helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153825				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>line styles;defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;line styles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	sh	\<variable id=\"linestyle_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/linestyle_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Line Styles\"\>Defining Line Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	sh	Select a line drawing object in a document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419	14			0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - \</emph\>\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<emph\>Drawing Object\</emph\> - \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<emph\>Graphic - \</emph\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"/\>\<emph\>Line\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Line Styles\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155449				0	sh	Specify the line options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	sh	To specify the length of the line as a percentage of the line width, select \<emph\>Fit to line width\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	sh	Enter a name for the line style and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3149202				0	sh	To save the line style in a custom line style list, click the \<emph\>Save Line Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\linestyle_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10671				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> to close the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Copying Graphics Between Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	sh	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	sh	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	sh	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	sh	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	sh	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	sh	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	sh	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	sh	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	sh	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Registering and Deleting a Database 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	sh	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	sh	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	sh	To register an existing database file:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	sh	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
