helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3155450				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3152349\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152349\"\>This icon is for tips on how to use the program more effectively.\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	sh	The document is saved under its path and name on the current local data medium or network drive or on the Internet, overwriting any file of the same name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3150984				0	sh	When you save a new file for the first time, the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"Save As\"\>Save As\</link\> dialog opens, in which you can enter a name, folder and drive or volume for the file. To open this dialog, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_save.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	sh	You can set the automatic creation of a backup copy under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Load/Save - General\"\>Load/Save - General\</link\>\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
