helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	sh	\<variable id=\"border_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_table.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\"\>Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	sh	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	sh	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	sh	Click one of the predefined border styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	sh	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	sh	Setting a Customized Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	sh	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	sh	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	sh	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	sh	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	sh	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	sh	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting Charts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>charts; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>plotting data as charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; editing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; chart data\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	sh	\<variable id=\"chart_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Charts\"\>Inserting Charts\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3139133				0	sh	Different methods exist to start a chart:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6772972				0	sh	Insert a chart based on data from cells in Calc or Writer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6049684				0	sh	These charts update automatically when the source data changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2356944				0	sh	Insert a chart with a default data set, and then use the Data Table dialog to enter your own data for that chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id866115				0	sh	These charts can be created in Writer, Impress and Draw. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146763				0	sh	Copy a chart from Calc or Writer into another document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id701315				0	sh	These charts are snapshots of the data at the time of copying. They do not change when the source data changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4439832				0	sh	In Calc, a chart is an object on a sheet, it cannot be a sheet of its own.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id719931				0	sh	Chart in a Calc spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	sh	Click inside the cell range that you want to present in your chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7211218				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Insert Chart\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7549363				0	sh	You see a chart preview and the Chart Wizard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9091769				0	sh	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> to create the chart. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3761406				0	sh	Chart in a Writer text document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066	32			0	sh	In a Writer document, you can insert a chart based on the values in a Writer table. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id428479				0	sh	Click inside the Writer table. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7236243				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - Chart\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6171452				0	sh	You see a chart preview and the Chart Wizard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	7			0	sh	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> to create the chart. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id6436658				0	sh	Chart based on values of its own				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6944792				0	sh	In Writer, if you have not selected any cells, choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - Chart\</emph\> to insert a chart with default data. In Draw or Impress, choose \<emph\>Insert - Chart\</emph\> to insert a chart based on default data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	sh	You can change the default data values by double-clicking on the chart and then choosing \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"View - Chart Data Table\"\>\<emph\>View - Chart Data Table\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
