helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154422				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>spadmin\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; adding, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>default printer; UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard printer under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>faxes; fax programs/fax printers under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; faxes under UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PostScript; PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converters; PostScript, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF; PostScript to PDF converter, UNIX\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147834				0	sh	\<variable id=\"spadmin\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/spadmin.xhp\" name=\"Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\"\>Setting up Printer and Fax Under UNIX Based Platforms\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159876				0	sh	%PRODUCTNAME uses the installed fonts of your system. In a text document you can select from all printable fonts. In an HTML document or in Web layout, only fonts that are visible on screen are offered. In spreadsheets and drawings you can select from all installed fonts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	sh	Under UNIX based platforms, the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> is provided to help you set up printers and faxes for use with the $[officename] software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	sh	Call the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	sh	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	sh	Enter: ./spadmin				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	sh	After it starts, the window of the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\> appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	sh	Following a server installation, the system administrator first logs on as with root privileges, and starts the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>. The administrator then creates a general printer configuration file called {install_path}/share/psprint/psprint.conf for all users. All changes are immediately available to all users.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159177				0	sh	Setting up Printers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	sh	Under UNIX based platforms, the $[officename] software only offers direct support for printers using the PostScript technology. Other printers must be set up as described in the section \<emph\>Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software\</emph\>. The $[officename] software automatically provides a printer with the default driver for each system queue. You can add additional printers as needed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148564				0	sh	Adding a Printer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147559				0	sh	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	sh	Enter: ./spadmin				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Create Printer\</emph\> option and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	sh	Select the appropriate driver for your printer. If you are not using a PostScript printer or your model is not listed, use the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> driver or follow the steps below. You can also add new drivers using the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> button or delete unnecessary drivers using the \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	sh	Choose a command line that you can use to print on your printer (for example, lp -d my_queue). Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	sh	Give the printer a name and determine whether it should become the default printer. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	sh	To print a test page, click on \<emph\>Test Page\</emph\>. If the test page fails to print or is incorrectly printed, check all settings as described in \<emph\>Changing Printer Settings\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146147				0	sh	Printer Drivers in the $[officename] Software				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	sh	When installing a non-PostScript printer, you must set your system so that PostScript can be converted into the language of the printer. We recommend using current PostScript conversion software such as Ghostscript (http://www.cs.wisc.edu/~ghost/).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154639				0	sh	You should set up the \<emph\>Generic Printer\</emph\> in that case. Also make sure that the page margins are set correctly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	sh	If you are using a printer using the PostScript technology, you should install a description file for the printer (PostScript Printer Definition - PPD) so that you can utilize the specific printer features like paper tray selection, duplex print function and all built-in fonts. You can also use the generic printer driver since it contains the most important data and is suitable for most printers. In that case, you will have to do without the paper tray selection and must correctly set the page margins.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976	128			0	sh	Some PPD files are installed as default files. If there is no matching PPD file for your printer, you will find various PPD files at http://www.adobe.com/products/printerdrivers/. You can also ask the manufacturer of your printer for PPD files. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147435				0	sh	Importing Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149484				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Import\</emph\> in the driver selection dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260	347			0	sh	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> to select the directory where you unpacked the PPD files. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147443				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Selection of drivers\</emph\> list box, select the printer driver you want to install.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	sh	Click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152885				0	sh	Deleting Drivers When Creating a New Printer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	sh	Select the printer driver.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149909				0	sh	Be sure that you do not delete the generic printer driver, and remember that drivers deleted from server installations are no longer available to other users who are using the same server installation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	sh	If the printer has more fonts built in than the usual PostScript fonts, you must also load the AFM files for these additional fonts. Copy the AFM files into the {install_path}/share/psprint/fontmetric directory or into the {install_path}/user/psprint/fontmetric directory. You can find AFM files, for example, at ftp://ftp.adobe.com/pub/adobe/type/win/all/afmfiles/.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148388				0	sh	Changing Printer Settings				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	sh	In the printer administration program \<emph\>spadmin\</emph\>, select the printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box and click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog appears containing several tab pages. This is where you can make settings that are used according to the PPD file of the selected printer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148833				0	sh	Select the command on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. You can remove superfluous commands using the \<emph\>Remove\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154270				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Paper\</emph\> tab page, you can define the paper format and paper tray to be used as the default settings for this printer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145649				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Device\</emph\> tab page, you can activate the special options for your printer. If your printer can only print in black and white, choose "grayscale" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\>, otherwise choose "color". If switching to grayscale leads to unfavorable results, you can also select "color" under \<emph\>Color\</emph\> and see how the printer or PostScript emulator applies it. Furthermore, on this tab page you can set the precision with which colors are described as well as the PostScript level.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	sh	The \<emph\>Font Replacement\</emph\> tab page allows you to select a printer font type available in the printer for each font type installed on your computer. This way you can reduce the data volume sent to the printer. Font replacement can be turned on or off for each printer individually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	sh	You should also set the page margins correctly on the \<emph\>Additional settings\</emph\> tab when using the generic printer driver so that your printout is not cropped. You can also enter a description in the Comments field, which will also be displayed on the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	sh	Some of these settings can also be set for the current printout in the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog or the \<emph\>Printer Settings\</emph\> dialog in the $[officename] software with the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	sh	Renaming or Deleting Printers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	sh	Select a printer from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	sh	To rename the selected printer, click \<emph\>Rename\</emph\>. Enter an appropriate name in the dialog that appears and click OK. The name must be unique and should be chosen so that you can recognize the printer and the application. Printer names must be assigned the same for all users because, when documents are exchanged, the selected printer remains unchanged if the recipient has it under the same name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	sh	To delete the selected printer, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>. The default printer or a printer that has been created by the system administrator in a server installation cannot be removed using this dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Selecting a Default Printer \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	sh	To make the printer selected from the \<emph\>Installed printers\</emph\> list box the default printer, double-click its name or click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154204				0	sh	Using Fax Functionality				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463				0	sh	If you have installed a fax package such as Efax or HylaFax on your computer, you can send faxes with the $[officename] software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154575				0	sh	Change to the {install_path}/program directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	sh	Enter: ./spadmin				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146808				0	sh	Click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3151070				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Connect a fax device\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150787				0	sh	Choose whether to use the default driver or another printer driver. If you are not using the default driver, select the appropriate driver. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	sh	Enter a command line with which to communicate with the fax in the following dialog. In the command line of each fax sent "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(PHONE)" by the telephone number of the recipient fax machine. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the PostScript code is transmitted in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	sh	Assign a name to your new fax printer and determine whether the telephone numbers (see below) marked in the text should be removed from the printout, or not. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	sh	You can now send faxes by printing to the printer that has just been created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3148419				0	sh	Enter the fax number as text in the document. You can also enter a field that takes the fax number from your active database. In any case, the fax number must start with the characters @@# and end with @@. A valid entry would have the form @@#1234567@@.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150826				0	sh	If these characters including the telephone number are not printed, activate the \<emph\>Fax number is removed from the printout\</emph\> option under \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> on the \<emph\>Command\</emph\> tab page. If no telephone number is entered in the document, a dialog prompting you for it will appear after the printout.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	sh	In $[officename] you can also activate an icon for sending faxes to a default fax. To do this, choose \<emph\>Tools - Customize - Toolbars\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Add Commands\</emph\> and add from "Documents" the \<emph\>Send Default Fax\</emph\> icon. You can set which fax is used when this button is pressed under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	sh	Remember to create one separate print job for each fax, otherwise, the first recipient will receive all the faxes. In the \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge\</emph\> dialog select the \<emph\>Printer\</emph\> option and then select the \<emph\>Single print jobs\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146929				0	sh	Connecting a PostScript to PDF Converter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3154989				0	sh	If a PostScript to PDF converter such as Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is installed on your computer, you can quickly create PDF documents in the $[officename] software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3150524				0	sh	In spadmin, click \<emph\>New Printer\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Add Printer\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3145268				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Connect a PDF converter\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	sh	Choose whether to use the default driver, the Acrobat Distiller driver or another driver. The driver "Generic Printer (T42 enabled)" prefers the type 42 fonts over type 3 fonts; this driver is a good choice for output to a software PostScript interpreter. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3155128				0	sh	In the next dialog, enter a command line for the PostScript->PDF Converter. Enter the directory where the PDF files should be saved. If you do not provide a directory, the user's home directory will be used. In the command line "(TMP)" is replaced by a temporary file and "(OUTFILE)" by the target file, the name of which is created from the document name. If "(TMP)" occurs in the command line, the Postscript code is forwarded in a file, otherwise as standard input through a pipe. If Ghostscript or Adobe Acrobat Distiller is in the search path, you can use one of the predefined command lines. Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	sh	Assign a name to your new PDF converter. Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\spadmin.xhp	0	help	par_id3153064				0	sh	You can now create PDF documents by printing to the converter that has just been created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Using Context Menus				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>context menus\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>menus;activating context menus\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; context menus\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>activating;context menus\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\contextmenu.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	sh	\<variable id=\"contextmenu\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/contextmenu.xhp\" name=\"Using Context Menus\"\>Using Context Menus\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Recording Changes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>changes; recording\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recording; changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>comments; on changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>review function;tracking changes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	sh	\<variable id=\"redlining_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_enter.xhp\" name=\"Recording Changes\"\>Recording Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7271645				0	sh	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145669				0	sh	Not all changes are recorded. For example, the changing of a tab stop from align left to align right is not recorded. However, all usual changes made by a proofreader are recorded, such as additions, deletions, text alterations, and usual formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	sh	1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	sh	To start recording changes, open the document to be edited and choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Changes\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Changes\</emph\>\</link\> and then choose \<emph\>Record\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749				0	sh	2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	sh	Now start making your changes. You will note that all new text passages that you enter are underlined in color, while all text that you delete remains visible but is crossed out and shown in color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	sh	3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	sh	If you move to a marked change with the mouse pointer, you will see a reference to the type of change, the author, date and time of day for the change in the Help Tip. If the Extended Tips are also enabled, you will also see any available comments on this change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156119				0	sh	Changes in a spreadsheet document are highlighted by a border around the cells; when you point to the cell you can see more detailed information on this change in the Help Tip.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	sh	You can enter a comment on each recorded change by placing the cursor in the area of the change and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Comment\</emph\>. In addition to Extended Tips, the comment is also displayed in the list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153542				0	sh	To stop recording changes, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> again. The check mark is removed and you can now save the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153627				0	sh	In a text document, you can highlight all lines that you have changed with an additional colored marking. This can be in the form of a red line in the margin, for example.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147530				0	sh	To change the settings for tracking changes, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040700.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\> or on the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060600.xhp\" name=\"Changes\"\>\<emph\>Changes\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149180				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>page formats; maximizing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; maximizing page formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printers; maximum page formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149180				0	sh	\<variable id=\"pageformat_max\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pageformat_max.xhp\" name=\"Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page\"\>Selecting the Maximum Printable Area on a Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	sh	Not all printers can print a paper up to its edges. Most of them leave an unprinted margin.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	sh	$[officename] offers a semi-automatic feature that enables you to print as close to the paper's edge as is possible.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	sh	Make sure that your printer has been setup under \<emph\>File - Printer Settings\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	sh	Make sure that the \<emph\>Web Layout\</emph\> in the \<emph\>View\</emph\> menu is not selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	sh	Select the \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> command, and go to the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	sh	Under \<emph\>Margins\</emph\> you can define the maximum or minimum possible value for the page margins (left, right, top, and bottom). Click into the respective control, then press the Page Up or Page Down key. The preview displays a dashed line around the printable range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing\"\>Printing\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
