helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	sh	The links \<emph\>And, Or\</emph\> and \<emph\>Exactly\</emph\> are available.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150358				0	sh	Prefix				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_URL\"\>This text box displays the URL and the first part of the query command for a search machine. A URL can also be typed directly.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153193				0	sh	Suffix				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153970				0	sh	The search terms are passed between the prefix and the suffix.\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_POSTFIX\"\>The suffix provides the command sequence, sent at the end of a search.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	sh	Separator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:EDIT:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_SEPARATOR\"\>If you type more than one word while running a search, these words will be separated by the character specified here.\</ahelp\> Most search engines require the "+" character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149560				0	sh	To determine which prefixes, separators and suffixes to use when defining a new search engine:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159255				0	sh	Activate the search engine and perform a search with at least two words.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	sh	Copy the URL from your browser's \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field and paste it into a blank document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148647				0	sh	Change the conditions for the search in the search engine, if it offers you the choice.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	sh	Again, copy the contents of the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147213				0	sh	Compare the URLs with the sample URLs in the fields of this dialog and make a note of the prefixes, suffixes and separators used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	sh	Case match				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154918				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:ED_CASE\"\>Determines the case match for running a search.\</ahelp\> The list contains the following entries: \<emph\>None\</emph\>, \<emph\>Upper\</emph\> and \<emph\>Lower\</emph\>. The search terms entered are converted according to your selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	sh	Search engines handle queries differently according to the way they are constructed. For example, some are case sensitive and some are not. Because of this, it is best to select \<emph\>None\</emph\> as the case match option.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156283				0	sh	New				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149413				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:PUSHBUTTON:RID_SVXPAGE_INET_SEARCH:PB_NEW\"\>Use this button to include a new search engine.\</ahelp\>\<emph\>New\</emph\> deletes all important entries of the entry mask such as "Name" and "Suffix". Enter the new search engine together with all of the necessary details. As soon as you accept your entries with \<emph\>Add\</emph\>, the new search engine will appear in the search engine list under \<emph\>Search in\</emph\>. Close the dialog with the \<emph\>OK\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01020200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145254				0	sh	Add				20181231 09:50:43
