helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id2016968				0	sh	Default file format and ODF settings				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id2659077				0	sh	ODF format version				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id6944181				0	sh	OpenOffice.org 3 and StarOffice 9 introduce new features which have to be saved using the \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenDocument\"\>OpenDocument\</link\> format (ODF) version 1.2. The prior versions of OpenOffice.org 2 and StarOffice 8 support the file formats ODF 1.0/1.1. Those prior file formats cannot store all new features of the new software.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id886257				0	sh	Current versions can open documents in ODF formats 1.0/1.1 and 1.2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id8892483				0	sh	When you save a document, you can select whether to save the document in the format ODF 1.2, ODF 1.2 (Extended), or in the prior format ODF 1.0/1.1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200911205367				0	sh	Currently, the ODF 1.2 (Extended) format enables files of Draw and Impress to contain comments. Those comments can be inserted by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Comment\</item\> in the latest software version. The comments get lost when loading files into prior software versions that were saved by the latest software version.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id7198400				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Some companies or organizations may require ODF documents in the ODF 1.0/1.1 format. You can select that format to save in the listbox. This older format cannot store all new features, so the new format ODF 1.2 (Extended) is recommended where possible.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164920				0	sh	File encryption algorithm for ODF 1.2 format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3160488	78			0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_ODFENCRYPTION\"\>Change the default file encryption from blowfish to AES-256 when ODF 1.2 is used.\</ahelp\> The default file encryption algorithm is blowfish but when ODF 1.2 is used the user can change the default to AES-256. Older encrypted documents can still be loaded but new encrypted documents can't be opened with older office versions. The AES-256 algorithm is more secure than blowfish.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154920				0	sh	Size optimization for ODF format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_CHECKBOX_RID_SFXPAGE_SAVE_BTN_NOPRETTYPRINTING\"\>When saving the document, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> writes the XML data without indents and extra line breaks.\</ahelp\> This allows documents to be saved and opened more quickly, and the file size is smaller.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091E				0	sh	Warn when not saving in ODF or default format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>You can choose to get a warning message when you save a document in a format that is not OpenDocument or which you did not set as default format in \<emph\>Load/Save - General\</emph\> in the Options dialog box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01010200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158444				0	sh	You can choose which file format will be applied as the default when saving documents of various document types. If you always exchange your documents with other persons who use Microsoft Office, for example, you may specify here that %PRODUCTNAME only uses the Microsoft Office file formats as a default.				20181231 09:50:43
