helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Mark to enable the automatic check for updates. Choose %PRODUCTNAME - Online Update in the Options dialog box to disable or enable this feature.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id0116200901063996				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select a folder to download the files.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id6797082				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>You can check for updates manually or automatically.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id4218878				0	sh	Checking for updates will also look for updates of all installed extensions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id8132267				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Help - Check for Updates\</item\> to check manually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id702230				0	sh	You can disable or enable the automatic check in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/online_update.xhp\"\>Online Update\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3422345				0	sh	If an update is available, an icon\<image id=\"img_id3155415\" src=\"extensions/source/update/ui/onlineupdate_16.png\" width=\"0.4583in\" height=\"0.1354in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155415\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the menu bar will notify you of the update. Click the icon to open a dialog with more information.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id9313638				0	sh	You will see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/online_update_dialog.xhp\"\>Check for Updates\</link\> dialog with some information about the online update of %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id9951780				0	sh	Enable an Internet connection for %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id6479384				0	sh	If you need a proxy server, enter the proxy settings in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Internet - Proxy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3639027				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Check for Updates\</item\> to check for the availability of a newer version of your office suite.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id3722342				0	sh	If a newer version is available and %PRODUCTNAME is not set up for automatic downloading, then you can select any of the following actions:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id5106662				0	sh	Download the new version.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id4931485				0	sh	Install the downloaded files.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	sh	Abort this check for updates for now.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	sh	If %PRODUCTNAME is configured to download the files automatically, the download starts immediately. A download continues even when you minimize the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id927152				0	sh	If automatic downloads are disabled, start the download manually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	sh	If no update was found, you can close the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\online_update.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	sh	You need Administrator rights to update %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	HTML import and export				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154380				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>importing; HTML with META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; META tags in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tags; META tags\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154380				0	sh	HTML import and export				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	sh	When you export a file to an HTML document, the description and the user-defined file properties are included as META \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> between the HEAD tags of the exported document. META tags are not displayed in a Web browser, and are used to include information, such as keywords for search engines on your Web page. To set the properties of the current document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> or \<emph\>User Defined\</emph\> tabs, and then type the information you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	sh	The following file properties are converted to META tags when you export a file as an HTML document:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154935				0	sh	File Property				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	sh	<TITLE>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3153778				0	sh	Subject				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	sh	<META NAME="CLASSIFICATION" CONTENT="Field Content">				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	sh	Keywords				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	sh	<META NAME="KEYWORDS" CONTENT="Field Content">				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	sh	Description				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	sh	<META NAME="DESCRIPTION" CONTENT="Field Content">				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	sh	Info fields 1...4				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3157892				0	sh	<META NAME="Info field name" CONTENT="Field Content">				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	22			0	sh	When you import an HTML containing these META tags, the contents of the tags are added to the corresponding $[officename] file property box. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id0926200812164481				0	sh	Keywords must be separated by commas. A keyword can contain white space characters or semicolons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822				0	sh	Import Tips				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307				0	sh	When you import an HTML document, following META tags are automatically converted to $[officename] fields: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> and <META NAME="..." ...> , where NAME equals to AUTHOR, CREATED, CHANGED, CHANGEDBY, DESCRIPTION, KEYWORDS or CLASSIFICATION.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	sh	Scripts, comments, and META tags that are positioned directly before a TABLE tag are inserted in the first cell of the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	sh	Scripts and META tags in the header of an HTML document are imported and anchored to the first paragraph in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	sh	To set the options for importing HTML tags, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. A known META tag contains either "HTTP-EQUIV" or "NAME", and are imported as $[officename] comments. The only exception is <META NAME="GENERATOR"...>, which is ignored.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717				0	sh	Export Tips				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180				0	sh	Comments and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				20181231 09:50:43
