helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147366				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05110000.xhp\" name=\"Style\"\>Style\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	sh	Use this command to quickly apply font styles to a text selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153255				0	sh	If you place the cursor in a word and do not make a selection, the font style is applied to the entire word. If the cursor is not inside a word, and no text is selected, then the font style is applied to the text that you type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Comment				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154100				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>comments;inserting/editing/deleting/printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing; comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>records; inserting comments \</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks, see also comments\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154100				0	sh	Comment				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151100				0	sh	\<variable id=\"notizbearbeitentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertAnnotation\"\>Inserts a comment.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id9851680				0	sh	Inserting comments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id1830500				0	sh	In Writer, the command \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Comment\</item\> or the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C key combination inserts a comment anchor at the current cursor position. A comment box is shown at the page margin, where you can enter the text of your comment. A line connects anchor and comment box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0915200910571516				0	sh	In Calc, Draw, and Impress, the command \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Comment\</item\> inserts a comment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id1831				0	sh	The author name and the date and time of creating this comment is shown at the bottom of the comment box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6718649				0	sh	The comments by different authors get different colors. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</item\> to enter your name so that it can show up as the comment author.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id2929166				0	sh	Editing comments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5201879				0	sh	Every user with write permission to the document can edit and delete comments of all authors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id2571794				0	sh	The comment box contains an icon with a down arrow. Click the icon to open a menu with some commands to delete comments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0522200809383431				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Delete the current comment.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0522200809383485				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Delete all comments by this author in the current document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0522200809383428				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Delete all comments in the current document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id1857051				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Choose a command to delete the current comment, or all comments from the same author as the current comment, or all comments in the document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911090684				0	sh	If the comment in a text document was written by another author, there is a Reply command in the context menu. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>This command inserts a new comment adjacent to the comment to which you want to reply.\</ahelp\> The comment anchor is the same for both comments. Type your reply text in the new comment. Save and send your document to other authors, then those authors can add replies, too.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0804200803435883				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Comments\</item\> to show or hide all comments (not available in Calc).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200901430918				0	sh	In the Find & Replace dialog of text documents, you can select to include the comments texts in your searches.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3445539				0	sh	Navigating from comment to comment in text documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id4271370				0	sh	When the cursor is inside a comment, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Down to jump to the next comment, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up to jump to the previous comment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id2116153				0	sh	When the cursor is inside the normal text, press the above mentioned keys to jump to the next or previous comment anchor. You can also use the small Navigation window below the vertical scrollbar to jump from one comment anchor to the next comment anchor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5381328				0	sh	You can also open the Navigator to see a list of all comments. Right-click a comment name in the Navigator to edit or delete the comment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5664235				0	sh	Printing comments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id2254402				0	sh	To change the printing option for comments for all your text documents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0915200910571612				0	sh	Comments in spreadsheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	sh	When you attach a comment to a cell, a callout appears where you can enter your text. A small square in the upper right corner of a cell marks the position of a comment. To display the comment permanently, right-click the cell, and choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id8336741				0	sh	To change the object properties of a comment, for example the background color, choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> as above, then right-click the comment (do not double-click the text).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390				0	sh	To edit a shown comment, double-click the comment text. To edit a comment that is not shown permanently, click in the cell that contains the comment, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>. To specify the formatting of the comment text, right-click the comment text in edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A1				0	sh	To change the position or size of a comment, drag a border or corner of the comment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id9499496				0	sh	To delete a comment, right-click the cell, then choose \<emph\>Delete Comment\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id2036805				0	sh	You can also right-click a comment name in the Navigator window to choose some editing commands.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153716				0	sh	To set the printing options for comments in your spreadsheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id2419507				0	sh	In Impress, you can choose to use the Notes view to write a page of notes for every slide. Additionally, you can insert comments to your slides. 				20181231 09:50:43
