helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Sets the display properties of a grid.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057E				0	sh	Display Grid				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_idN10582				0	sh	Displays or hides grid lines that you can use to align objects such as graphics on a page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_idN10585				0	sh	Snap to Grid				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_idN10589				0	sh	Automatically aligns objects to vertical and horizontal grid lines. To override this feature, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you drag an object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C9				0	sh	Grid to Front				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CD				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the grid lines in front of the objects on the slide or page.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\grid.xhp	0	help	par_id4372692				0	sh	Set the grid color on \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\"\>Appearance\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Position				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150467				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050600.xhp\" name=\"Position\"\>Position\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id3158397				0	sh	Sets the indent, spacing, and alignment options for the numbered or bulleted list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06050600.xhp	0	help	par_id5004119				0	sh	The Position tab page looks different for documents using the new position and spacing attributes introduced with OpenOffice.org 3.0, or documents using the old attributes from versions before 3.0. The new version of this tab page shows the controls "Numbering followed by", "Numbering alignment", "Aligned at", and "Indent at". The old version of this tab page that can be seen in an old numbered or bulleted list shows the controls "Indent", "Width of numbering", "Minimum space numbering <-> text", and "Numbering alignment".				20181231 09:50:43
