helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152472				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Delete spaces and tabs at beginning and end of paragraph\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Removes spaces and tabs at the beginning of a paragraph. To use this option, the \<emph\>Apply Styles\</emph\> option must also be selected.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147303				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Delete blanks and tabs at end and start of lines\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150866				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Removes spaces and tabs at the beginning of each line. To use this option, the \<emph\>Apply Styles\</emph\> option must also be selected.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	sh	Ignore double spaces				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	sh	Replaces two or more consecutive spaces with a single space.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145116				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Apply numbering - symbol\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>Automatically creates a numbered list when you press Enter at the end of a line that starts with a number followed by a period, a space, and text. If a line starts with a hyphen (-), a plus sign (+), or an asterisk (*), followed by a space, and text, a bulleted list is created when you press Enter.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>To cancel automatic numbering when you press Enter at the end of a line that starts with a numbering symbol, press Enter again.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	sh	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157962				0	sh	Apply border				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144445				0	sh	Automatically applies a border at the base of the preceding paragraph when you type three or more specific characters, and then press Enter. To create a single line, type three or more hyphens (-), or underscores ( _ ), and then press Enter. To create a double line, type three or more equal signs (=), asterisks (*), tildes (~), or hash marks (#), and then press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C2E				0	sh	To delete the created line, click the paragraph above the line, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\>, delete the bottom border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\06040100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C35				0	sh	The following table summarizes the line thickness for the different characters: 				20181231 09:50:43
