helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149929				0	sh	Entering Dates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3148397				0	sh	To enter a date in a cell, use the Gregorian calendar format. For example, in an English locale, enter 1/2/2002 for Jan 2, 2002.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153274				0	sh	All date formats are dependent on the locale that is set in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language settings - Languages\</emph\>. For example, if your locale is set to 'Japanese', then the Gengou calendar is used. The default date format in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> uses the Gregorian Calendar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020301.xhp	0	help	par_id3153795				0	sh	To specify a calendar format that is independent of the locale, add a modifier in front of the date format. For example, to display a date using the Jewish calendar format in a non-Hebrew locale, enter: [~jewish]DD/MM/YYYY.				20181231 09:50:43
