helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1511581				0	sh	After inserting fields in the Detail view, the report is ready for execution.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4881740				0	sh	To execute a report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8286385				0	sh	Click the Execute Report icon\<image id=\"img_id3380230\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_executereport.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3380230\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2354197				0	sh	A Writer document opens and shows the report you have created, which contains all values of the database table which you have insert.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2485122				0	sh	If the database contents did change, execute the report again to update the result report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id8746910				0	sh	To edit a report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	sh	First decide if you want to edit the generated report, which is a static Writer document, or if you want to edit the Report Builder view and then generate a new report based on the new design.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	sh	The Writer document is opened read-only. To edit the Writer document, click Edit File\<image id=\"img_id8237556\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_editdoc.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8237556\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8307138				0	sh	If you want to edit the Report Builder view, you can change some of its properties.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7138889				0	sh	Click in the Details area. Then in the Properties window, change some properties, for example the background color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id9869380				0	sh	After finishing, click the Execute Report icon\<image id=\"Graphic2\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_executereport.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a new report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id12512				0	sh	If you close the Report Builder, you will be asked if the report should be saved. Click Yes, give the report a name, and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2676168				0	sh	Sorting the report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2626422				0	sh	Without sorting or grouping, the records will be inserted into the report in the order in which they are retrieved from the database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id1743827				0	sh	Open the Report Builder view and click the Sorting and Grouping icon\<image id=\"img_id9557786\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbsortingandgrouping.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9557786\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the toolbar. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	sh	In the Groups box, click the field which you want as the first sort field, and set the Sorting property.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	sh	Execute the report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	sh	Grouping				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	sh	Open the Report Builder view and click the Sorting and Grouping icon\<image id=\"Graphic21\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbsortingandgrouping.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the toolbar. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	sh	In the Groups box, open the Group Header list box and select to show a group header.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	sh	Click the Add Field icon\<image id=\"Graphic3\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_addfield.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Add Field window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id5675527				0	sh	Drag-and-drop the field entry that you want to group into the group header section. Then drag-and-drop the remaining fields into the Detail section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	sh	Execute the report. The report shows the grouped records.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	sh	If you like to sort and group, open the Report Builder view, then open the Sorting and Grouping dialog. Select to show a Group Header for the fields that you want to group, and select to hide the Group Header for the fields that you want to be sorted. Close the Sorting and Grouping window and execute the report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id888698				0	sh	Updating and printing your data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	sh	When you insert some new data or edit data in the table, a new report will show the updated data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	sh	Click the Reports icon\<image id=\"img_id4678487\" src=\"dbaccess/res/reports_32.png\" width=\"0.566cm\" height=\"0.566cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4678487\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and double-click your last saved report. A new Writer document will be created which shows the new data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_main.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	sh	To print a report, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\> from the Writer document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Generated Values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10553				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabaadvpropgen.xhp\"\>Generated Values\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10563				0	sh	Specifies the options for automatically generated values for new data records.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_id7684560				0	sh	The availability of the following controls depends on the type of database:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN1058C				0	sh	Retrieve generated values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10590				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enables $[officename] support for auto-incremented data fields in the current ODBC or JDBC data source. Select this option if the auto-increment feature in the SDBCX layer of the database is not supported. In general, the auto-increment is selected for the primary key field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10593				0	sh	Auto-increment statement				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10597				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the SQL command specifier that instructs the data source to auto-increment a specified Integer data field.\</ahelp\> For example, the following MySQL statement used the AUTO_INCREMENT statement to increase the "id" field each time the statement creates a data field:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A0				0	sh	CREATE TABLE "table1" ("id" INTEGER AUTO_INCREMENT)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10634				0	sh	For this example, you must enter AUTO_INCREMENT into the \<emph\>Auto-increment statement\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN105AA				0	sh	Query of generated values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter an SQL statement that returns the last auto-incremented value for the primary key data field.\</ahelp\> For example:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaadvpropgen.xhp	0	help	par_idN105B1				0	sh	SELECT LAST_INSERT_D();				20181231 09:50:43
