helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C0				0	sh	Using a Database in %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10838				0	sh	To create a new database file, choose \<emph\>File - New - Database\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083B				0	sh	The \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabawiz00.xhp\"\>Database Wizard\</link\> helps you to create a database file and to register a new database within %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	sh	The database file contains queries, reports, and forms for the database as well as a link to the database where the records are stored. Formatting information is also stored in the database file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084A				0	sh	To open a database file, choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>. In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> list box, select to view only "Database documents". Select a database document and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
