helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaprop.xhp	0	help	par_idN10560				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the properties of a database.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\dabaprop.xhp	0	help	par_id1322977				0	sh	In a database window, choose \<emph\>Edit - Database - Properties\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Join Properties				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154015				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>links;relational databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inner joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>joins in databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>left joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>full joins (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154015				0	sh	Join Properties				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3151205				0	sh	If you double-click a connection between two linked fields in the query design, or if you choose \<emph\>Insert - New Relation\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Join Properties\</emph\> dialog appears. These properties will be used in all queries created in the future.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155066				0	sh	Tables involved				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3153924				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_RIGHT_TABLE\"\>Specifies two different tables that you want to join.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	sh	Fields involved				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3148994				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies two data fields that will be joined by a relation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159267				0	sh	Options				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	sh	Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>Specifies the link type of the selected link.\</ahelp\> Some databases support only a subset of the possible types.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155334				0	sh	Inner Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the internal join, the results table contains only the records for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link is created by a corresponding WHERE clause.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156372				0	sh	Left Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the left join, the results table contains all fields of the left table and only those fields of the right table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the LEFT OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155607				0	sh	Right Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150647				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the right join, the results table contains all fields of the right table and only those fields of the left table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the RIGHT OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158215				0	sh	Full Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>For a full join, the results table contains all fields of the left and right tables.\</ahelp\> In the SQL of $[officename] this type of link corresponds to the FULL OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200912031976				0	sh	Natural				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200912031977				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts the keyword NATURAL into the SQL statement that defines the relation. The relation joins all columns that have the same column name in both tables. The resulting joined table contains only one column for each pair of equally named columns.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Sorting and Grouping				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3486434				0	sh	\<variable id=\"rep_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the Sorting and Grouping dialog of \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\>, you can define the fields that should be sorted in your report, and the fields that should be kept together to form a group.\</ahelp\> If you group your report by a certain field, all records with the same value of that field will be kept together in one group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id876186				0	sh	The Groups box shows the fields in an order from top to bottom. You can select any field, then click the Move Up or Move Down button to move this field up or down in the list. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	sh	The sorting and grouping will be applied in the order of the list from top to bottom.				20181231 09:50:43
