helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1150852				0	sh	You can open the Report Navigator window of the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Builder\</link\> by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Report Navigator\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1111484				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Report Navigator reveals the structure of the report. You can use the Report Navigator to insert functions into the report.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id8314157				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an entry in the Report Navigator. The corresponding object or area is selected in the Report Builder view. Right-click an entry to open the context menu.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id2932828				0	sh	To enter functions to the report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the context menu of the Report Navigator, you see the same commands as in the Report Builder view, plus additional commands to create new functions or to delete them.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	sh	Functions can be entered using a syntax as specified by the \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenFormula\"\>OpenFormula\</link\> proposal.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4095583				0	sh	See \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Database\"\>Wiki page about Base\</link\> for some more help regarding the functions in a report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id311593				0	sh	To calculate a sum for each client				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3948789				0	sh	Open the Report Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5391399				0	sh	Open the Groups entry and the group where you want to calculate the cost. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6989654				0	sh	The group has a sub entry called functions. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1803643				0	sh	Open the context menu (right click) on the functions entry, choose to create a new function, and select it. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id868251				0	sh	In the property browser you see the function. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6247749				0	sh	Change the name to e.g. CostCalc and the formula to [CostCalc] + [enter your cost column name].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1565904				0	sh	In the initial value enter 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1569261				0	sh	Now you can insert a text field and bind it to your [CostCalc] (appears in the data field list box).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9256874				0	sh	Maybe you have to set the initial value to the value of the field like [field].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4601886				0	sh	If there are blank fields in the cost column, use the following formula to replace the blank fields' content with zero:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1754509				0	sh	[SumCost] + IF(ISBLANK([field]);0;[field])				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the formula that defines the function. Use OpenFormula syntax.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the initial value for the evaluation of the formula. Often this is set to 0 or to 1.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Deep traversing is enabled, functions are evaluated considering all lower levels of hierarchy. This would be used for instance for line numbering. If Deep traversing is not enabled, only the first level of hierarchy is evaluated.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Pre evaluation is enabled, functions are evaluated only when the report is finished.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
