helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Data Point				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Data Point\"\>Data Point\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	sh	This dialog allows you to change the properties of a selected data point. The dialog appears when there is only one data point selected when you choose \<emph\>Format - Format Selection\</emph\>. Some of the menu entries are only available for 2D or 3D charts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149121				0	sh	Any changes made only affect this one data point. For example, if you edit the color of a bar, only the color of that bar will be different.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Smooth Line Properties				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	bm_id3803827				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>curves;properties in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>properties;smooth lines in line charts/XY charts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id3050325				0	sh	Smooth Line Properties				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id9421979				0	sh	In a chart that displays lines (Line type or XY type), you can choose to show curves instead of straight lines. Some options control the properties of those curves.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	hd_id1228370				0	sh	To change line properties				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1601611				0	sh	Select Cubic Spline or B-Spline.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id879848				0	sh	These are mathematical models that influence the display of the curves. The cubic spline line passes through all points, while the B-spline line connects the first and last point and passes by the intermediate points.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3464461				0	sh	Optionally set the resolution. A higher value leads to a smoother line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id6998809				0	sh	For B-spline lines optionally set the data points order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a cubic spline model.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id1068758				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Apply a B-spline model.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id2320932				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the resolution.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\smooth_line_properties.xhp	0	help	par_id8638874				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Set the data points order.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
