helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id2003845				0	sh	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id7757194				0	sh	XY (Scatter)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	sh	An XY chart in its basic form is based on one data series consisting of a name, a list of x‑values, and a list of y‑values. Each value pair (x|y) is shown as a point in a coordinate system. The name of the data series is associated with the y‑values and shown in the legend.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	sh	Choose an XY chart for the following example tasks:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	sh	scale the x‑axis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	sh	generate a parameter curve, for example a spiral				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	sh	draw the graph of a function				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	sh	explore the statistical association of quantitative variables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	sh	Your XY chart may have more than one data series.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5461897				0	sh	XY Chart Variants				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	sh	You can choose an XY chart variant on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\>, or by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Chart Type \</item\>for a chart in edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	sh	The chart is created with default settings. After the chart is finished, you can edit its properties to change the appearance. Line styles and icons can be changed on the \<emph\>Line\</emph\>tab page of the data series properties dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5482039				0	sh	Double-click any data point to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Series\</item\> dialog. In this dialog, you can change many properties of the data series.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200810492449				0	sh	For 2D charts, you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</item\> to enable the display of error bars.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6221198				0	sh	You can enable the display of mean value lines and trend lines using commands on the Insert menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id1393475				0	sh	Points only				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6571550				0	sh	Each data point is shown by an icon. %PRODUCTNAME uses default icons with different forms and colors for each data series. The default colors are set in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Charts - Default Colors\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5376140				0	sh	Lines Only				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4408093				0	sh	This variant draws straight lines from one data point to the next. The data points are not shown by icons. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7261268				0	sh	The drawing order is the same as the order in the data series. Mark \<emph\>Sort by X Values\</emph\> to draw the lines in the order of the x values. This sorting applies only to the chart, not to the data in the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6949369				0	sh	Points and Lines				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	sh	This variant shows points and lines at the same time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6765953				0	sh	3D Lines				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7422711				0	sh	The lines are shown like tapes. The data points are not shown by icons. In the finished chart choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\> to set properties like illumination and angle of view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id239265				0	sh	Smooth Lines				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7957396				0	sh	Mark \<emph\>Smooth Lines\</emph\> to draw curves instead of straight line segments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1202124				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> to set details for the curves.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5989562				0	sh	\<emph\>Cubic Spline\</emph\> interpolates your data points with polynomials of degree 3. The transitions between the polynomial pieces are smooth, having the same slope and curvature. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6128421				0	sh	The \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> determines how many line segments are calculated to draw a piece of polynomial between two data points. You can see the intermediate points if you click any data point.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9280373				0	sh	\<emph\>B-Spline\</emph\> uses the data points as control points to form a B-spline curve. Those curves are built piecewise from polynomials. The \<emph\>Data points order\</emph\> sets the degree k of these polynomials. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Chart Wizard - Chart Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	bm_id4266792				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>charts;choosing chart types\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
