helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150199				0	sh	Rotate				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148489				0	sh	Rotates or skews the selected 2D object(s) around a pivot point. Drag a corner handle of the object in the direction you want to rotate it. To skew an object, drag a center handle in the direction you want to skew it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	sh	Each slide has only one pivot point. Double-click an object to move the pivot point to the center of the object. You can also drag the pivot point to a new location on the screen, and then rotate the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	sh	If you select a group that includes a 3D object, only the 3D object is rotated. You cannot skew a 3D object, instead, you can rotate it about the X and Y axes by dragging the center handles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3153811\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectrotatemode.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153811\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
