helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149875				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10080000.xhp\" name=\"Curve\"\>Curve\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147301				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:LineToolbox\"\>The Curve icon on the Drawing bar opens the \<emph\>Lines\</emph\> toolbar, where you can add lines and shapes to the current slide.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157873				0	sh	If you hold the Shift key down, the movement of the mouse is limited to multiples of 45 degrees. If you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Options\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, the new point will not be connected to the last point. This allows you to create objects that consist of curves that are not connected together. If you draw a smaller object while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key into a larger object that you have not closed yet, the smaller object is subtracted from the larger one, thus appearing as a hole in the larger one.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153083	8			0	sh	Closed shapes automatically receive the fill that is displayed in the \<emph\>Area Style/Filling\</emph\> box on \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155926				0	sh	Curve, Filled				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150016				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:BezierFill\"\>Draws a filled closed shape that is based on a Bézier curve. Click where you want the curve to start, drag, release, and then move the pointer to where you want the curve to end and click. Move the pointer and click again to add a straight line segment to the curve. Double-click to close the shape.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148773				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3150936\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_bezierfill.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150936\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570				0	sh	Curve, Filled				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149028	9			0	sh	Polygon, filled 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155374				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Polygon\"\>Draws a closed shape consisting of straight line segments. Click where you want to start the polygon, and drag to draw a line segment. Click again to define the end of the line segment, and continue clicking to define the remaining line segments of the polygon. Double-click to finish drawing the polygon. To constrain the polygon to angles of 45 degree, hold down Shift when you click.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\02\10080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153720				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3083443\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_polygon.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3083443\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
