helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	About Layers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>layers; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	sh	\<variable id=\"layers\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layers.xhp\" name=\"About Layers\"\>About Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	sh	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	sh	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	sh	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	sh	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	sh	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	sh	Layout				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	sh	Controls				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	sh	Dimension Lines				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	sh	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	sh	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	sh	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	sh	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	sh	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D scenes; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	sh	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	sh	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	sh	Curved object based on Bézier curves				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	sh	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	sh	3D object with shading and a light source				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	sh	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	sh	Two types of 3D objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	sh	The Status bar displays "3D scene selected". The 3D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y, and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3D objects. When exporting these 3D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3D bars in charts are of this type, too.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	sh	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2D mode or in a 3D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2D or 3D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	sh	To convert an object to a curved shape:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	sh	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	sh	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	sh	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	sh	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	sh	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	sh	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	sh	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	sh	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	sh	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	sh	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	sh	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon\<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	sh	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	sh	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147506				0	sh	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151318				0	sh	Right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D Rotation Object\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3146125				0	sh	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the Line and Filling toolbar and the 3D Settings toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149336				0	sh	You can rotate the 2D object before converting it to create a more complex shape.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Creating a Custom Slide Show				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; always with the current slide\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting;custom slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;hidden slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden pages;showing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	sh	\<variable id=\"individual\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/individual.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Custom Slide Show\"\>Creating a Custom Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	sh	You can create custom slide shows to meet the needs of your audience using slides within the current presentation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	sh	To create a custom slide show:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153712				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Shows\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966	62			0	sh	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and enter a name for your slide show in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150249				0	sh	Under \<emph\>Existing Slides\</emph\>, select the slides you want to add to your slide show, and click the \<emph\>>>\</emph\> button. Hold down Shift to select a range of slides, or Ctrl to select multiple slides.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	sh	You can change the order of the slides in your custom slide show, by dragging and dropping the slides under \<emph\>Selected Slides\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151387				0	sh	To start a custom slide show:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	sh	Select the show you want to start from the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3149943				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Start\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145593	56			0	sh	If you want the selected custom slide show to start when you click the \<emph\>Slide Show\</emph\> icon on the\<emph\> Presentation\</emph\> toolbar, or when you press F5, select \<emph\>Use Custom Slide Show\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145169				0	sh	Options for Running a Slide Show				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150335				0	sh	To always start a slide show from the current slide:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150014				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155932				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Start presentation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3155372				0	sh	Do not select this option if you want to run a custom slide show.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153922				0	sh	To hide a slide:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id883150344				0	sh	To hide the current slide, click the Hide Slide action button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	sh	To hide several slides, choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the slide(s) that you want to hide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3083278				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3151264				0	sh	The slide is not removed from your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147570				0	sh	To show a hidden slide:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3145210				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>, and then select the hidden slide(s) that you want to show.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\individual.xhp	0	help	par_id3150260				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Show/Hide Slide\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Creating Animated GIF Images				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153188				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; creating cross-fades\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images; animating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>animated GIFs\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153188				0	sh	\<variable id=\"animated_gif_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/animated_gif_create.xhp\" name=\"Creating Animated GIF Images\"\>Creating Animated GIF Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	sh	You can animate drawing objects, text objects, and graphic objects (images) on your slides to make your presentation more interesting. $[officename] Impress provides you with a simple animation editor where you can create animation images (frames) by assembling objects from your slide. The animation effect is achieved by rotating through the static frames that you create.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	sh	If you create a bitmap animation (animated GIF), you can assign a delay time to each frame, and specify the number of times the animation is played.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150250				0	sh	To create an animated GIF:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148703	59			0	sh	Select an object or group of objects that you want to include in your animation and choose\<emph\> Insert - Animated Image\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086	97			0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Apply Object \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3148489\" src=\"sd/res/get1obj.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148489\"\>Note Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to add a single object or a group of objects to the current animation frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150860	98			0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Apply Objects Individually \</emph\>button \<image id=\"img_id3149355\" src=\"sd/res/getallob.png\" width=\"0.423cm\" height=\"0.423cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149355\"\>Tip Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to create a separate animation frame for each of the selected objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148391	61			0	sh	In the \<emph\>Animation Group \</emph\>area, select \<emph\>Bitmap object\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154871				0	sh	Use the animation timeline to specify the duration for displaying a frame and the number of times an animation sequence is presented (looping).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154644				0	sh	Enter a frame number in the \<emph\>Image Number\</emph\> box (left box).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150756	63			0	sh	Enter the number of seconds you want the frame to display in the \<emph\>Duration \</emph\>box (middle box).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151182				0	sh	Repeat the last two steps for each frame in your animation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177	100			0	sh	You can preview your animation by using the controls to the left of the \<emph\>Image Number \</emph\>box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939	65			0	sh	Select the number of times you want the animation sequence to repeat in the \<emph\>Loop count \</emph\>box (right box).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\animated_gif_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145421				0	sh	Select an alignment option for the objects in the \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
