helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803040964				0	sh	In Impress and Draw, you can connect each two shapes with a line called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\"\>connector\</link\>. When you draw a connector between shapes, the connector will be attached to a gluepoint on each shape. Each shape has some default gluepoints, and the positions of the default gluepoints depend on the specific shape. You can add your own custom gluepoints to a shape and then attach connectors to the custom gluepoints.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041099				0	sh	To add and edit gluepoints				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id091920080304108				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041082				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Drawing toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041186				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Glue Points\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041160				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Gluepoints toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041115				0	sh	Click inside the shape where you want to add the new gluepoint.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041133				0	sh	If the shape is filled, you can click anywhere inside the shape. If the shape is unfilled, you can click the border to insert a glue point. Once inserted, you can drag the glue point to another position inside the shape.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041250				0	sh	With the four icons next to the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon, you choose the directions which will be permitted for a connector at this gluepoint. You can choose one or more directions for a particular gluepoint.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041298				0	sh	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is active, the gluepoint moves when you resize the object to keep its position relative to the object borders.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041223				0	sh	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is not active, the icons next to it are no longer grayed out. With these icons you can decide where a gluepoint will be placed when the size of the object is changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Selecting Underlying Objects				20181231 09:50:43
