helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	sh	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	sh	Select a rectangular range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	sh	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	sh	Mark a single cell				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	sh	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	sh	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. Release the mouse button. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	sh	Select various dispersed cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	sh	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	sh	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	sh	Switch marking mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	sh	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	sh	Field contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	sh	Effect of clicking the mouse				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	sh	STD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	sh	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	sh	EXT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305				0	sh	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked. Alternatively, Shift-click a cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	sh	ADD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	sh	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click the cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Defining Database Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>tables; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; defining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; defining database ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;database ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758				0	sh	\<variable id=\"database_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Database Ranges\"\>Defining a Database Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	sh	You can define a range of cells in a spreadsheet to use as a database. Each row in this database range corresponds to a database record and each cell in a row corresponds to a database field. You can sort, group, search, and perform calculations on the range as you would in a database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	82			0	sh	You can only edit and access a database range in the spreadsheet that contains the range. You cannot access the database range in the %PRODUCTNAME Data Sources view. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10648				0	sh	To define a database range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	sh	Select the range of cells that you want to define as a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10654				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Define Range\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066A				0	sh	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	sh	Specify the options for the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10675				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Applying Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759				0	sh	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	sh	Inserting a Sheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a color to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	sh	Selecting Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	sh	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>you can select multiple sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	sh	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	sh	Undoing a Selection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	sh	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	sh	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	sh	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Creating Pivot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491				0	sh	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating Pivot Tables\"\>Creating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	sh	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Create\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	sh	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	sh	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	sh	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	sh	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	sh	Use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Field\</item\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key while clicking the desired calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	sh	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	sh	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	sh	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	sh	Exit the Pivot Table dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The pivot table is inserted further down.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	sh	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	sh	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	sh	To format numbers with decimals:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	sh	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	sh	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Deactivating Automatic Changes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	sh	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	sh	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	sh	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	sh	Automatic Text or Number Completion				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	sh	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	sh	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	sh	Automatic Conversion to Date Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	sh	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	sh	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	sh	Quotation Marks Replaced by Custom Quotes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Localized Options\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	sh	Cell Content Always Begins With Uppercase				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab. Unmark \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	sh	Replace Word With Another Word				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Delete\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Entering Fractions 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	sh	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	sh	You can enter a fractional number in a cell and use it for calculation:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	sh	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	sh	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Options\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	sh	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells. \</emph\>Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Copying Formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113				0	sh	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulas\"\>Copying Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	sh	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	sh	Select the cell containing the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	sh	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	sh	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	sh	Select the cell containing the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	sh	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	sh	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	sh	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	sh	If you do not want values and texts to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulas, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Copying to Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	sh	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	sh	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	sh	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	sh	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	sh	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Updating Pivot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	sh	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating Pivot Tables\"\>Updating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	sh	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the pivot table. To recalculate the table, choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Applying AutoFilter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>filters, see also AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function;applying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; filter values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; filter sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drop-down menus in sheet columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	sh	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	sh	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	sh	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	sh	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	sh	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	sh	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	sh	To display all records again, select the "all\<emph\>"\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose "Standard\<emph\>"\</emph\>, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Standard Filter\</item\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose "Top 10" to display the highest 10 values only. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	sh	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	sh	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	sh	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Protecting Cells from Changes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	sh	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Cells from Changes\"\>Protecting Cells from Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	sh	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulas can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	sh	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	sh	Note that the cell protection for cells with the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute is only effective when you protect the whole sheet. In the default condition, every cell has the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute. Therefore you must remove the attribute selectively for those cells where the user may make changes. You then protect the whole sheet and save the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	sh	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidental action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	sh	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	sh	Select the protection options that you want. All options will be applied only after you protect the sheet from the Tools menu - see below.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id31529866655				0	sh	Uncheck \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to allow the user to change the currently selected cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	sh	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulas from changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	sh	Apply the protection options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	sh	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialog, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	sh	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	sh	(Optional) Enter a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	sh	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	13			0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
