helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	sh	Pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys inserts a manual line break. This shortcut only works directly in the cell, not in the input line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	sh	If you want the text to automatically break at the right border of the cell, proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	sh	Select all the cells where you want the text to break at the right border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	sh	In \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\> option and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
