helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D7				0	sh	\<variable id=\"printranges\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F5				0	sh	You can define which range of cells on a spreadsheet to print.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FB				0	sh	The cells on the sheet that are not part of the defined print range are not printed or exported. Sheets without a defined print range are not printed and not exported to a PDF file, unless the document uses the Excel file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	sh	For files opened in Excel format, all sheets that do not contain a defined print range are printed. The same behavior occurs when you export the Excel formatted spreadsheet to a PDF file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	sh	To Define a Print Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	sh	Select the cells that you want to print.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10909				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10910				0	sh	To Add Cells to a Print Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	sh	Select the cells that you want to add to the existing print range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091B				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	sh	To Clear a Print Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10929				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Remove\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	sh	Using the Page Break Preview to Edit Print Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centered page number in gray. Nonprinting areas have a gray background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	sh	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	sh	To View and Edit Print Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10937				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	sh	To change the default zoom factor of the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, double click the percentage value on the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> bar, and select a new zoom factor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10836				0	sh	Edit the print range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10944				0	sh	To change the size of a print range, drag a border of the range to a new location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	sh	To delete a manual page break that is contained in a print range, drag the border of the page break outside of the print range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10948				0	sh	To clear a print range, drag a border of the range onto the opposite border of the range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	sh	To exit the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
