helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	sh	\<variable id=\"calc_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Calculating Series\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	sh	You can automatically fill cells with data with the AutoFill command or the Series command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D3				0	sh	Using AutoFill				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D7				0	sh	AutoFill automatically generates a data series based on a defined pattern.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	sh	On a sheet, click in a cell, and type a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	sh	Click in another cell and then click back in the cell where you typed the number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	sh	Drag the fill handle in the bottom right corner of the cell across the cells that you want to fill, and release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	sh	The cells are filled with ascending numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	sh	To quickly create a list of consecutive days, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Monday\</item\> in a cell, and drag the fill handle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9720145				0	sh	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	sh	If you select two or more adjacent cells that contain different numbers, and drag, the remaining cells are filled with the arithmetic pattern that is recognized in the numbers. The AutoFill function also recognizes customized lists that are defined under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	sh	You can double-click the fill handle to automatically fill all empty columns of the current data block. For example, first enter Jan into A1 and drag the fill handle down to A12 to get the twelve months in the first column. Now enter some values into B1 and C1. Select those two cells, and double-click the fill handle. This fills automatically the data block B1:C12.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	sh	Using a Defined Series				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	sh	Select the cell range in the sheet that you want to fill.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Fill - Series\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	sh	Select the parameters for the series. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	sh	If you select a \<emph\>linear\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>added\</emph\> to each consecutive number in the series to create the next value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073C				0	sh	If you select a \<emph\>growth\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>multiplied\</emph\> by each consecutive number to create the next value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10747				0	sh	If you select a \<emph\>date\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is added to the time unit that you specify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3159173				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
