helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Importing and Exporting Text Files				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulas as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	sh	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	sh	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	sh	To Import a CSV File				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	sh	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	sh	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	sh	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	sh	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	sh	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	sh	If you want to export the formulas as formulas, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	sh	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	sh	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Save as\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	sh	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	sh	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	sh	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	sh	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	sh	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting and Editing Comments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	sh	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	sh	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	sh	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	sh	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	sh	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	sh	Move or resize each comment as you like.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	sh	Format each comment by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	sh	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	sh	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>Insert - Comment\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Naming Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; defining for cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>values; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>constants definition\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;names for cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; defining names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell names; defining/addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; by defined names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>allowed cell names\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>renaming;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	sh	\<variable id=\"value_with_name\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/value_with_name.xhp\" name=\"Naming Cells\"\>Naming Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id4391918				0	sh	Allowed names				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2129581				0	sh	Names in Calc can contain letters, numeric characters, and some special characters. Names must start with a letter or an underline character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id1120029				0	sh	Allowed special characters:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3362224				0	sh	underline (_) 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4891506				0	sh	period (.) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id2816553				0	sh	blank ( ) - allowed within a name, but not as first or last character, and not for a cell range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id328989				0	sh	Names must not be the same as cell references. For example, the name A1 is invalid because A1 is a cell reference to the top left cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id32898987				0	sh	Names must not start with the letter R followed by a number. See the ADDRESS function for more information.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4769737				0	sh	Names for cell ranges must not include blanks. Blanks are allowed within names for single cells, sheets and documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	hd_id1226233				0	sh	Naming cells and formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5489364				0	sh	A good way of making the references to cells and cell ranges in formulas legible is to give the ranges names. For example, you can name the range A1:B2 \<emph\>Start\</emph\>. You can then write a formula such as "=SUM(Start)". Even after you insert or delete rows or columns, $[officename] still correctly assigns the ranges identified by name. Range names must not contain any spaces.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id953398				0	sh	For example, it is much easier to read a formula for sales tax if you can write "= Amount * Tax_rate" instead of "= A5 * B12". In this case, you would name cell A5 "Amount" and cell B12 "Tax_rate."				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id4889675				0	sh	Use the \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog to define names for formulas or parts of formulas you need more often. In order to specify range names,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	sh	Select a cell or range of cells, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Define Names\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	sh	Type the name of the selected area in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> field. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>. The newly defined name appears in the list below. Click OK to close the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id5774101				0	sh	You can also name other cell ranges in this dialog by entering the name in the field and then selecting the respective cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154942				0	sh	If you type the name in a formula, after the first few characters entered you will see the entire name as a tip.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	sh	Press the Enter key in order to accept the name from the tip.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	sh	If more than one name starts with the same characters, you can scroll through all the names using the Tab key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\value_with_name.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04070100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Names - Define\"\>Insert - Names - Define\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
