helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155089				0	sh	Reduce/enlarge printout				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	sh	Specifies a scaling factor to scale all printed pages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN1099A				0	sh	Scaling factor				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_id3152899				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SC_METRICFIELD_RID_SCPAGE_TABLE_ED_SCALEALL\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a scaling factor. Factors less than 100 reduce the pages, higher factors enlarge the pages.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B2				0	sh	Fit print range(s) to width/height				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B5				0	sh	Specifies the maximum number of pages horizontally (width) and vertically (height) on which every sheet with the current Page Style is to be printed. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BB				0	sh	The print ranges are always scaled proportionally, so the resulting number of pages may be less than specified.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109BF				0	sh	You may clear one of the boxes, then the unspecified dimension will use as many pages as necessary.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05070500.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C3				0	sh	If you clear both boxes, this will result in a scaling factor of 100%.				20181231 09:50:43
