helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149012				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>WORKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149012				0	sh	\<variable id=\"workday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_workday.xhp\"\>WORKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_WORKDAY\"\> The result is a date number that can be formatted as a date. You then see the date of a day that is a certain number of \<emph\>workdays\</emph\> away from the \<emph\>start date\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146944				0	sh	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	sh	WORKDAY(StartDate; Days; Holidays)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3147469				0	sh	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the date from when the calculation is carried out. If the start date is a workday, the day is included in the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153038				0	sh	\<emph\>Days\</emph\> is the number of workdays. Positive value for a result after the start date, negative value for a result before the start date.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	sh	\<emph\>Holidays\</emph\> is a list of optional holidays. These are non-working days. Enter a cell range in which the holidays are listed individually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150141				0	sh	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3152782				0	sh	What date came 17 workdays after 1 December 2001? Enter the start date "2001-12-01" in C3 and the number of workdays in D3. Cells F3 to J3 contain the following Christmas and New Year holidays: "2001-12-24", "2001-12-25", "2001-12-26", "2001-12-31", "2002-01-01".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_workday.xhp	0	help	par_id3146142				0	sh	=WORKDAY(C3;D3;F3:J3) returns 2001-12-28. Format the serial date number as a date, for example in the format YYYY-MM-DD.				20181231 09:50:43
