helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1939451				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to shrink or restore the dialog. You can click or select cells in the sheet. You can enter a cell reference manually in the input box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to remove the row from the list. Any rows from below this row move up.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Options dialog.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to solve the equation with the current settings. The dialog settings are retained until you close the current document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5474410				0	sh	To solve equations with the solver				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	sh	The goal of the solver process is to find those variable values of an equation that result in an optimized value in the \<emph\>target cell\</emph\>, also named the "objective". You can choose whether the value in the target cell should be a maximum, a minimum, or approaching a given value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	sh	The initial variable values are inserted in a rectangular cell range that you enter in the \<emph\>By changing cells\</emph\> box. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	sh	You can define a series of limiting conditions that set constraints for some cells. For example, you can set the constraint that one of the variables or cells must not be bigger than another variable, or not bigger than a given value. You can also define the constraint that one or more variables must be integers (values without decimals), or binary values (where only 0 and 1 are allowed).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5323953				0	sh	The default solver engine supports only linear equations.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	DATE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155511				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>DATE function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155511				0	sh	\<variable id=\"date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_date.xhp\"\>DATE\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153551				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATUM\"\>This function calculates a date specified by year, month, day and displays it in the cell's formatting.\</ahelp\> The default format of a cell containing the DATE function is the date format, but you can format the cells with any other number format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148590				0	sh	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150474				0	sh	DATE(Year; Month; Day)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152815				0	sh	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9957 or between 0 and 99.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153222				0	sh	In \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General \</item\>you can set from which year a two-digit number entry is recognized as 20xx.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155817				0	sh	\<emph\>Month\</emph\> is an integer indicating the month.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	sh	\<emph\>Day\</emph\> is an integer indicating the day of the month.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	sh	If the values for month and day are out of bounds, they are carried over to the next digit. If you enter \<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;12;31)\</item\> the result will be 12/31/00. If, on the other hand, you enter \<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;13;31)\</item\> the result will be 1/31/01.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	sh	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152589				0	sh	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DATE(00;1;31)\</item\> yields 1/31/00 if the cell format setting is MM/DD/YY.				20181231 09:50:43
