helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	sh	\<emph\>StartDate\</emph\> is the first date				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3146324				0	sh	\<emph\>EndDate\</emph\> is the second date				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	sh	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> calculates the type of difference. The possible values are 0 (interval) and 1 (in numbers of weeks).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145237				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKSINYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of weeks;in a specific year\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145237				0	sh	WEEKSINYEAR				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147410				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DAI_FUNC_WEEKSINYEAR\"\>Calculates the number of weeks of the year in which the date entered occurs.\</ahelp\> The number of weeks is defined as follows: a week that spans two years is added to the year in which most days of that week occur.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149719				0	sh	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3145638				0	sh	WEEKSINYEAR(Date)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149946				0	sh	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> is any date in the respective year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150037				0	sh	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3147614				0	sh	WEEKSINYEAR(A1) returns 53 if A1 contains 1970-02-17, a valid date for the year 1970.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157901				0	sh	Add-ins through %PRODUCTNAME API				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3149351				0	sh	Add-ins can also be implemented through the %PRODUCTNAME \<link href=\"https://api.openoffice.org/\"\>API\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
