helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:RecalcPivotTable\"\>Updates the pivot table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	sh	After you import an Excel spreadsheet that contains a pivot table, click in the table, and then choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Refresh\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Protect Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148946				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060000.xhp\" name=\"Protect Document\"\>Protect Document\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153362	2			0	sh	The\<emph\> Protect Document \</emph\>command prevents changes from being made to cells in the sheets or to sheets in a document. As an option, you can define a password. If a password is defined, removal of the protection is only possible if the user enters the correct password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147228				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060100.xhp\" name=\"Sheets\"\>Sheets\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153768				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06060200.xhp\" name=\"Documents\"\>Documents\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10622				0	sh	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp#cell_protect\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Protecting Sheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	sh	Protecting Sheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	sh	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	sh	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	sh	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	sh	Select the cells that will be unprotected				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	sh	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	sh	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	sh	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	sh	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	sh	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	sh	Password (optional)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	sh	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Cell Protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145119				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Cell Protection\"\>Cell Protection\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\05020600.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCPAGE_PROTECTION\"\>Defines protection options for selected cells.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
