helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150882				0	sh	ASINH(Number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147621	104			0	sh	 This function returns the inverse hyperbolic sine of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>, that is the number whose hyperbolic sine is Number. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153212				0	sh	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156120				0	sh	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASINH(-90)\</item\> returns approximately -5.1929877.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4808496				0	sh	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ASINH(SINH(4))\</item\> returns 4.				20181231 09:50:43
