helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	51			0	sh	            \<emph\>Mean\</emph\> is the arithmetic mean of the distribution.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874	52			0	sh	            \<emph\>StDev\</emph\> is the standard deviation of the distribution.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351				0	sh	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156067	54			0	sh	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=STANDARDIZE(11;10;1)\</item\> returns 1. The value 11 in a normal distribution with a mean of 10 and a standard deviation of 1 is as much above the mean of 10, as the value 1 is above the mean of the standard normal distribution.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157986				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>NORMSINV function\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>normal distribution;inverse of standard\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
