helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154950	68			0	sh	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value to which the standard normal cumulative distribution is calculated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228				0	sh	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984	70			0	sh	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=NORMSDIST(1)\</item\> returns 0.84. The area below the standard normal distribution curve to the left of X value 1 is 84% of the total area.				20181231 09:50:43
