helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	sh	You can create duplicate or multiple copies of an object. The copies can be identical or can differ in size, color, orientation and location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	sh	The following example creates a stack of coins by making multiple copies of a single ellipse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	sh	Use the \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> tool to draw a solid yellow ellipse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	sh	Select the ellipse and choose \<emph\>Edit - Duplicate\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145585	9			0	sh	Enter 12 as \<emph\>Number of copies.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151192				0	sh	Enter a negative value for the \<emph\>Width\</emph\> and \<emph\>Height\</emph\> so that the coins decrease in size as you go up the stack.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	sh	To define a color transition for the coins, select different colors in the \<emph\>Start\</emph\> and \<emph\>End\</emph\> boxes. The \<emph\>Start\</emph\> color is applied to the object that you are duplicating.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to create the duplicates.				20181231 09:50:43
