helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156443				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>combining; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>intersecting draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>polygons; intersecting/subtracting/merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subtracting polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>constructing shapes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443	64			0	sh	\<variable id=\"combine_etc\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/combine_etc.xhp\" name=\"Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\"\>Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020	65			0	sh	Combined drawing objects act as grouped objects, except that you cannot enter the group to edit the individual objects. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	sh	You can only combine 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	sh	To combine 2D objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	sh	Select two or more 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Combine\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	sh	Unlike groups, a combined object takes on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order. You can split apart combined objects, but the original object properties are lost.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155088				0	sh	When you combine objects, holes appear where the objects overlap.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	sh	 \<image id=\"img_id3157978\" src=\"res/helpimg/kombi1.png\" width=\"8.3646inch\" height=\"2.5inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3157978\"\>Illustration for combining objects\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	sh	In the illustration, the uncombined objects are on the left and the combined objects on the right.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159229				0	sh	Constructing Shapes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	sh	You can construct shapes by applying the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13180000.xhp\" name=\"Shapes\"\>\<emph\>Shapes\</emph\>\</link\> \<emph\>- Merge, Subtract and Intersect\</emph\> commands to two or more drawing objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	sh	Shape commands only work on 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150539				0	sh	Constructed shapes take on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156402				0	sh	To construct a shape:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3157874				0	sh	Select two or more 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Shapes\</emph\> and one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145829	91			0	sh	 \<emph\>Merge\</emph\> 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154680	92			0	sh	 \<emph\>Subtract\</emph\> 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153034				0	sh	 \<emph\>Intersect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145144				0	sh	Shape Commands				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	sh	In the following illustrations, the original objects are on the left and the modified shapes on the right.				20181231 09:50:43
