helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511				0	sh	If you want, you can mix a custom color and add it to a color table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	sh	To define a custom color				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Colors\</emph\> tab. A table of the predefined colors is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	sh	Changes made to the standard color table are permanent and are saved automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	sh	Click a color in the table that is similar to the one you want to mix. The color appears in the upper preview box to the right of the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	sh	Select the RGB or CMYK color model in the box below the preview boxes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id4979705				0	sh	%PRODUCTNAME uses only the RGB color model for printing in color. The CMYK controls are provided only to ease the input of color values using CMYK notation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152987	16			0	sh	The RGB color model mixes red, green and blue light to create colors on a computer screen. In the RGB model, the three color components are additive and can have values ranging from 0 (black) to 255 (white). The CMYK color model combines Cyan (C), Magenta (M), Yellow (Y), and blacK (K, also used for "Key") to create colors for printing. The four colors of the CMYK models are subtractive and are defined as percentages. Black corresponds to 100 % and white to 0 %.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145386				0	sh	Enter a numeric value in the boxes next to the color components. The new color appears in the preview box directly above the color model box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152871				0	sh	You can also create a color using a color spectrum. Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Color\"\>\<emph\>Color\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. Click a color. Use the Hue, Saturation, and Brightness boxes to adjust your color selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3147244				0	sh	If you want to replace the color in the standard color table that your custom color is based on, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	sh	If you want to add your custom color to the standard color table, enter a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> text box and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145236				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/03170000.xhp\" name=\"Color bar\"\>Color bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Cross-Fading Two Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150715				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; cross-fading two objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; two draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	sh	\<variable id=\"cross_fading\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/cross_fading.xhp\" name=\"Cross-Fading Two Objects\"\>Cross-Fading Two Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	sh	Cross-fading creates shapes and distributes them by uniform increments between two drawing objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112				0	sh	The cross-fading command is only available in $[officename] Draw. You can, however, copy and paste cross-faded objects into $[officename] Impress.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149209				0	sh	To cross-fade two objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	sh	Hold down Shift and click each object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cross-fading\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	sh	Enter a value to specify the number of objects between the start and end of the cross-fade in the \<emph\>Increments\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3149405				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	sh	A group containing the two original objects and the specified number (increments) of cross-faded objects is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/ueberblenden.png\" width=\"74.88mm\" height=\"65.62mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Illustration for crossfading\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	sh	You can edit the individual objects of a group by selecting the group and pressing F3. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F3 to exit the group editing mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Editing - Cross-fading\"\>Editing - Cross-fading\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656				0	sh	\<variable id=\"align_arrange\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/align_arrange.xhp\" name=\"Arranging and Aligning Objects\"\>Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	sh	Arranging Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727				0	sh	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object, proceed as follows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	sh	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	sh	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	sh	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	sh	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	sh	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	sh	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	sh	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	sh	Click the object whose position you want to change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	sh	Click the object behind which you want to place the selected object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789				0	sh	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	sh	Shift-click both objects to select them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425				0	sh	Aligning Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	sh	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	sh	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	sh	Distributing Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	sh	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	sh	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	sh	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	sh	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Grouping Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	sh	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	sh	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	sh	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	sh	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	sh	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	sh	To group objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	sh	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	sh	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002				0	sh	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	sh	Selecting Objects in a Group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	sh	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	sh	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				20181231 09:50:43
