helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	sh	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\"\>Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	sh	You can create and edit drawing objects using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	sh	To Create and Edit a Drawing Object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	sh	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	sh	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow key until you reach the toolbar icon of a drawing tool.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	sh	If there is an arrow next to the icon, the drawing tool opens a sub toolbar. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\> arrow key to open the sub toolbar, then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\> key to select an icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	sh	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	sh	The object is created at the center of the current document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	sh	To return to the document, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062				0	sh	You can use the arrow keys to position the object where you want. To choose a command from the context menu for the object, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F10\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150306				0	sh	To Select an Object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	sh	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6\</item\> to enter the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	sh	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> until you reach the object you want to select.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Drawing Sectors and Segments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	sh	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	sh	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	sh	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	sh	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	sh	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	sh	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361				0	sh	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	sh	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	sh	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	sh	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581				0	sh	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	sh	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20181231 09:50:43
