helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	sh	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	sh	Text in a text box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	sh	Text that changes character size to fill the frame size				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	sh	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	sh	Text that is copied from a Writer document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	sh	Text that is inserted from a text document or HTML document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	sh	Adding a Text Box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	sh	Drag a text box to the size you want in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	sh	Type or paste your text into the text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	sh	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text box to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437				0	sh	Fitting Text to Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	sh	Create a text box as described in the steps above.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	sh	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	sh	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155955				0	sh	Text Tied to a Graphic				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	sh	You can add text to any graphic after double-clicking the graphic.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	sh	To determine the position of the text, use the settings in \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147366	59			0	sh	For example, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Callouts\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154508\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_calloutshapes.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154508\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Callouts toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FD				0	sh	Select a callout and move the mouse pointer to where you want the callout to start.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150272				0	sh	Drag to draw the callout.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1978514				0	sh	Enter the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091A				0	sh	Copying Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10921				0	sh	Select the text in your Writer document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10925				0	sh	Copy the text to the clipboard (\<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092D				0	sh	Click the page or slide where you want to paste the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10931				0	sh	Paste the text using \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093C				0	sh	Using \<emph\>Paste special\</emph\>, you can choose the text format to be pasted. Depending on formats, you can copy different text attributes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093F				0	sh	Importing Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10946				0	sh	Click the page or slide where you want to import the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1094A				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10952				0	sh	Select a text file (*.txt) or an HTML file and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Insert Text\</emph\> dialog opens. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to insert the text.				20181231 09:50:43
