helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\19040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151173	2			0	sh	Click to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\> dialog. Click the arrow next to the icon and select the required field from the submenu. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\19040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154104				0	sh	You can select the following functions:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\19040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145248				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Other\"\>Other\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Combined Display				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/08080000.xhp\" name=\"Combined Display\"\>Combined Display\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151172				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatusBarFunc\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Displays current information about the active document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156375				0	sh	When the cursor is in a named section, the section name appears. When the cursor is in a table, the name of the table cell appears. The size of the object is shown when you edit frames or drawing objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145416				0	sh	When the cursor is positioned within text, you can double-click this field to open the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>\<emph\>Fields\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. In this dialog, you can define a field to be inserted in your document at the current cursor position. When the cursor is positioned in a table, a double-click in this field will call the \<emph\>Table Format\</emph\> dialog. Depending on the object selected, you can call up a dialog to edit a section, a graphic object, a floating frame, an OLE object, direct numbering or the position and size of a drawing object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\10020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Zoom Out				20181231 09:50:43
