helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\19020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148768				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"FN_INSERT_FOOTER\"\>Displays the footer of an HTML document if footers are enabled on the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05040400.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - Footer\"\>\<emph\>Format - Page - Footer\</emph\>\</link\> tab page.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Page Number				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145241				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/08010000.xhp\" name=\"Page Number\"\>Page Number\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151184				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:StatePageNumber\"\>The current page number is displayed in this field of the status bar. A double-click opens the Navigator, with which you can navigate in the document. A right-click shows all bookmarks in the document. Click a bookmark to position the text cursor at the bookmark location.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	sh	The displayed page (x) and the total number of pages (y) are shown in the form \<emph\>Page x/y\</emph\> When you scroll through a document with the mouse, the page number is displayed when you release the mouse button. When you scroll using the right scrollbar, the page numbers are displayed as a Help tip. The page numbering format of the status bar and scrollbar is identical.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417	3			0	sh	You can turn the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> display on or off by double-clicking the\<emph\> Page Number \</emph\>field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149806				0	sh	To go to a specific page, enter the page number in the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> spin button in the Navigator and then press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\02\08010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	sh	By pressing the shortcut keys Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F5, you switch to entering a page number. When you press Enter, the cursor moves to the selected page.				20181231 09:50:43
