helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	sh	You can only animate text that is contained in a drawing object, such as rectangles, lines, or text objects. For example, draw a rectangle, then double-click the rectangle and enter your text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	sh	Select the drawing object containing the text that you want to animate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Object - Text Attributes\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Animation\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Effect\</item\> box, select the animation that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	sh	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
