helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	sh	Use the AutoCorrect feature to remove line breaks that occur within sentences. Unwanted line breaks can occur when you copy text from another source and paste it into a text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153413	3			0	sh	This AutoCorrect feature only works on text that is formatted with the "Default" paragraph style. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138	5			0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>               \<emph\>.\</emph\>            				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab, ensure that \<emph\>Combine single line paragraphs if length greater than 50%\</emph\> is selected. To change the minimum percentage for the line length, double-click the option in the list, and then enter a new percentage.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145093				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	sh	Select the text containing the line breaks that you want to remove.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156253				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Apply Style\</item\> box on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar, choose “Default”.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\removing_line_breaks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153388				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - Apply\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147684				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>captions; adding chapter numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering; captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic numbering;of objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;chapter numbers in captions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147684				0	sh	\<variable id=\"captions_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\"\>Adding Chapter Numbers to Captions\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147395				0	sh	You can include chapter numbers in captions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147408				0	sh	Ensure that the text in your document is organized by chapters, and that the chapter titles and, if you want, the section titles, use one of the predefined heading paragraph styles. You must also assign a numbering option to the heading paragraph styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154249				0	sh	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527	19			0	sh	Select a caption title from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, and select a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> box. \<br/\>You also can enter a caption text in this dialog. If you want, enter text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Caption\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> box, select the number of heading levels to include in the chapter number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553				0	sh	Type the character that you want to separate the chapter number(s) from the caption number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Separator\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Caption\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226				0	sh	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
