helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149637				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; removing/interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists; interrupting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;removing/interrupting numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>interrupting numbered lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;starting numbers in lists\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149637				0	sh	\<variable id=\"numbering_paras\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_paras.xhp\" name=\"Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\"\>Modifying Numbering in a Numbered List\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3145092				0	sh	You can remove the numbering from a paragraph in a numbered list or change the number that a numbered list starts with.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id2172612				0	sh	If you want numbered headings, use the \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> menu command to assign a numbering to a paragraph style. Do not use the Numbering icon on the Formatting toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145107				0	sh	To Remove the Number From a Paragraph in a Numbered List				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3156248				0	sh	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph that you want to remove the numbering from.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153366				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	sh	To remove the number while preserving the indent of the paragraph, press the Backspace key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	sh	To remove the number and the indent of the paragraph, click the \<emph\>Numbering on/off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar. If you save the document in HTML format, a separate numbered list is created for the numbered paragraphs that follow the current paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154856				0	sh	To Change the Number That a Numbered List Starts With				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155877				0	sh	Click anywhere in the numbered list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3148691	22			0	sh	Enter the number you want the list to start with in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start \</item\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>at\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id3147116				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_paras.xhp	0	help	par_id6943571				0	sh	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Conditional Text for Page Counts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153108				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>page counts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text;page counts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153108				0	sh	\<variable id=\"conditional_text2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text2.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text for Page Counts\"\>Conditional Text for Page Counts\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156228				0	sh	You can create a conditional text field that displays the word "pages" instead of "page" in conjunction with a page count field if your document contains more than one page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	sh	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</item\>, and then enter a space.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	sh	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	sh	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page > 1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145280				0	sh	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Pages\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Then\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145305				0	sh	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Else\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Word Completion for Text Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>automatic word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>completion of words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function; word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;using/disabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>switching off;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deactivating;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>refusing word completions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rejecting word completions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	sh	\<variable id=\"word_completion\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076F				0	sh	$[officename] collects words that you frequently use in the current session. When you later type the first three letters of a collected word, $[officename] automatically completes the word. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	91			0	sh	If there is more than one word in the AutoCorrect memory that matches the three letters that you type, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to cycle through the available words. To cycle in the opposite direction, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Tab. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078D				0	sh	 To Accept/Reject a Word Completion				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN10794				0	sh	By default, you accept the word completion by pressing the Enter key. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079B				0	sh	 To reject the word completion, continue typing with any other key. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079E				0	sh	 To Switch off the Word Completion 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A5				0	sh	 Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AD				0	sh	 Clear \<emph\>Enable word completion\</emph\> . 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion.xhp	0	help	par_id7504806				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	sh	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	sh	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	sh	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	sh	To Define a Conditional Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	sh	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759				0	sh	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784				0	sh	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	sh	Click "Text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	sh	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	sh	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	sh	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	sh	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	sh	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	sh	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	sh	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	sh	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	sh	To Display the Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	sh	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	sh	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	sh	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	sh	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of conditional operators\"\>List of conditional operators\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; styles, by fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brush for copying styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; transferring\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	sh	\<variable id=\"stylist_fillformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fillformat.xhp\" name=\"Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\"\>Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	sh	You can quickly apply styles, such as paragraph and character styles, in your document by using the Fill Format Mode in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	sh	Click the icon of the style category that you want to apply.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	17			0	sh	Click the style, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fill Format Mode\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149644\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149644\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371				0	sh	Move the mouse pointer to where you want to apply the style in the document, and click. To apply the style to more than one item, drag to select the items, and then release.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	sh	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> when finished.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159259				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;protecting/unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting;tables and sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id6007263				0	sh	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</item\>\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id1924802				0	sh	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150114				0	sh	Protecting Sections in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	sh	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	sh	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	sh	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	sh	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	sh	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081				0	sh	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	sh	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	sh	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	sh	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	sh	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	sh	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	sh	Place the cursor in the cell or select the cells. First, if necessary, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>. Then right-click the cell to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Cell - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	sh	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	sh	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259				0	sh	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	sh	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	sh	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	sh	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	sh	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088				0	sh	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, mark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	sh	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	49			0	sh	Place the cursor in the index. First of all, if necessary, under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids \</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	sh	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	sh	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
