helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>settings;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;word completion settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>weekdays; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>months; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	hd_id4745017				0	sh	\<variable id=\"word_completion_adjust\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id4814294				0	sh	If you like it that $[officename] automatically completes the words that you frequently use, you can make further adjustments to refine that behavior. If you want, you can also save the current list of collected words so that it can be used in the next session.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2593462				0	sh	To fine-tune the word completion choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\> and select any of the following options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	sh	To Insert an Additional Space Character				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B03				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Append space\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	sh	The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	sh	To Define the Accept Key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	sh	Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D2				0	sh	To Select the Minimum Number of Characters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	sh	Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	sh	To Select the Scope of Collected Words				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4C				0	sh	Disable the option \<emph\>When closing a document, remove the words collected from it from the list\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	sh	Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	sh	If you enable the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	sh	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	sh	To Use the Word List for Further Sessions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	sh	If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	sh	Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	sh	Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	sh	The word completion feature collects the words.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	sh	Select all or some of the words in the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	sh	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy all selected words into the clipboard. Paste the clipboard into a new document and save it to get a reference list of collected words.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	sh	Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words.				20181231 09:50:43
