helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;master documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;creating/editing/exporting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subdocuments;creating/editing/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indexes; master documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	sh	\<variable id=\"globaldoc_howtos\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc_howtos.xhp\"\>Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id1522873				0	sh	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	sh	To Create a Master Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Master Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	sh	Open an existing document and choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	sh	If you are creating a new master document, the first entry in the Navigator should be a \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text\</item\> entry. Type an introduction or enter some text. This ensures that after having edited an existing style in the master document, you see the changed style when viewing the subdocuments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Navigator\</item\> for master documents (should open automatically, else press F5 to open), click and hold the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> icon, and do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	sh	To insert an existing file as a subdocument, choose \<emph\>File\</emph\>, locate the file that you want to include, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145405				0	sh	To create a new subdocument, choose \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, type a name for the file, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8550981				0	sh	To insert some text between subdocuments, choose \<emph\>Text\</emph\>. Then type the text. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	sh	To Edit a Master Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	sh	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	sh	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	sh	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	sh	To add text to a master document, right-click an item in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Text\</emph\>. A text section is inserted before the selected item in the master document where you can type the text that you want. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	sh	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move down\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move up\</item\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	sh	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	sh	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	sh	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	sh	To Start Each Subdocument on a New Page				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	sh	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	sh	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	sh	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	sh	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Flow\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Breaks\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then select “Page” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	sh	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	sh	To Export a Master Document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Text Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	sh	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8371227				0	sh	The subdocuments will be exported as sections. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Sections\</item\> to unprotect and remove sections, if you prefer a plain text document without sections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Printing a Brochure				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	bm_id6743064				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>printing; individual brochures\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>booklet printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brochures; printing individual\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F6				0	sh	\<variable id=\"print_brochure\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/print_brochure.xhp\"\>Printing a Brochure\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	sh	You can print a Writer document as a brochure or a booklet. That is, Writer prints two pages on each side of the paper, so that when you fold the paper, you can read the document as a book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DE				0	sh	When you create a document that you want to print as a brochure, use portrait orientation for the pages. Writer applies the brochure layout when you print the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	sh	To Print a Brochure				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10621				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B6				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070E				0	sh	In the properties dialog for your printer, set the paper orientation to landscape.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_id8947416				0	sh	If your printer prints duplex, and because brochures always print in landscape mode, you should use the "duplex - short edge" setting in your printer setup dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10628				0	sh	Return to \<emph\>Print\</emph\> dialog, and click the \<emph\>Page Layout\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN1062C				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Brochure\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10740				0	sh	For a printer that automatically prints on both sides of a page, specify to include "All pages".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\print_brochure.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EA				0	sh	If %PRODUCTNAME prints the pages in the wrong order, open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab page, select \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>, and then print the document again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Checking Spelling and Grammar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149684				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>spellcheck; checking text documents manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>checking spelling;manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>grammar checker\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149684				0	sh	\<variable id=\"spellcheck_dialog\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/spellcheck_dialog.xhp\" name=\"Checking Spelling and Grammar\"\>Checking Spelling and Grammar\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149814				0	sh	You can manually check the spelling and grammar of a text selection or the entire document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id0525200902184476				0	sh	To check the spelling and the grammar of a text, the appropriate dictionaries must be installed. For many languages three different dictionaries exist: a spellchecker, a hyphenation dictionary, and a thesaurus. Each dictionary covers one language only. Grammar checkers can be downloaded and installed as extensions. See the \<link href=\"https://extensions.openoffice.org/dictionary\"\>extensions web page\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149828				0	sh	The spellcheck starts at the current cursor position, or at the beginning of the text selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	sh	Click in the document, or select the text that you want to check.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Spelling and Grammar\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	sh	When a possible spelling error is encountered, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Spellcheck\</item\> dialog opens and $[officename] offers some suggested corrections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3149861				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	sh	To accept a correction, click the suggestion, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	sh	Edit the sentence in the upper text box, and then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	sh	To add the unknown word to a user-defined dictionary, click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3147107				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06010000.xhp\" name=\"Spellcheck dialog\"\>Spelling and Grammar dialog\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id9625843				0	sh	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Adding_More_Languages\"\>Wiki page: Adding more languages\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\spellcheck_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id1683706				0	sh	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Spellchecking_in_More_Languages\"\>Wiki page: Multiple language spellchecking\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
