helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	sh	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph where you want to change the page background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C1				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C9				0	sh	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D1				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box, select a page style that uses the page background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DB				0	sh	To change the background of the current page only, select a page style where the Next Style option is set to "Default".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DF				0	sh	To change the background of the current and subsequent pages, select a page style where the Next Style option is set to the name of the page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	sh	If you want to change the page background later on in the document, repeat steps 1 to 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E8				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
