helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	sh	Click in a word, or select the words in your document that you want to use as an index entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	sh	To change the text that appears in the index, type the text that you want in the \<emph\>Entry\</emph\> box. The text that you type here does not replace the selected text in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	sh	To add an index mark to similar words in your document, select \<emph\>Apply to all similar texts\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155889				0	sh	To add the entries to a custom index, click the \<emph\>New User-defined Index\</emph\> icon, enter the name of the index, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147119				0	sh	To Define Table of Contents Entries				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147132				0	sh	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150230				0	sh	To Use a Custom Paragraph Style as a Table of Contents Entry				20181231 09:50:43
