helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7253028				0	sh	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders and all inner lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9441206				0	sh	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7276833				0	sh	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5273293				0	sh	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5110019				0	sh	User defined settings				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1820734				0	sh	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7093111				0	sh	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3673818				0	sh	Line types				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2593768				0	sh	Image				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2055421				0	sh	Meaning				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9836115				0	sh	A black line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6485793				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id1237525\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1237525\"\>solid line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1454512				0	sh	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4618671				0	sh	A gray line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1239356				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id2688680\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_7.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2688680\"\>gray line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9474166				0	sh	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1545457				0	sh	A white line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1681875				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id7340617\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_8.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7340617\"\>white line for border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2316660				0	sh	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id5908688				0	sh	Examples				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5118564				0	sh	Select a single cell in a Writer table, then choose \<emph\>Table - Table properties - Borders\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id244758				0	sh	Select a thick line style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7741325				0	sh	To set a lower border, click the lower edge repeatedly until you see a thick line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id542313				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id4273506\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_wr_6.png\" width=\"1.4071in\" height=\"1.2555in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4273506\"\>setting thick lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2210760				0	sh	All cells in a Writer table have at least a left and a lower line by default. Most cells on the table perimeter have more lines applied by default. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5400860				0	sh	All lines that are shown in white in the preview will be removed from the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Rotating Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155911				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>text; rotating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rotating;text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	sh	\<variable id=\"text_rotate\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_rotate.xhp\" name=\"Rotating Text\"\>Rotating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147410				0	sh	You can only rotate text that is contained in a drawing object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153130				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars- Drawing\</item\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drawing\</item\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149866	68			0	sh	Select the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Text\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text\</item\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149600\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149600\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149590				0	sh	Drag in your document to draw the text object, and then type your text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154415	71			0	sh	Click outside of the object, then click the text you entered. Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/05090000.xhp\" name=\"Object Rotation Mode\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Rotate\</item\>\</link\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3145405\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectrotatemode.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145405\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drawing Object Properties\</item\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	sh	Drag one of the corner handles of the text object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	sh	You can also right-click the text object, choose \<emph\>Position and Size\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Rotation\</emph\> tab, and then enter a rotation angle or a new position for the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_rotate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Show Draw Functions\"\>Show Draw Functions\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147688				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>custom dictionaries; removing words from\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;words in user-defined dictionaries\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147688				0	sh	\<variable id=\"delete_from_dict\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/delete_from_dict.xhp\" name=\"Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\"\>Removing Words From a User-Defined Dictionary\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3151391				0	sh	Select the user-defined dictionary that you want to edit in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>User-defined\</item\> list, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\delete_from_dict.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	sh	Select the word that you want to delete in the \<emph\>Word\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	sh	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	sh	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	sh	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	sh	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	sh	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drag Mode\</item\> icon, and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert as Hyperlink\</item\> is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	sh	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	sh	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	sh	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	sh	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Creating a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147104				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; creating and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating; tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147104				0	sh	\<variable id=\"indices_toc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_toc.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Table of Contents\"\>Creating a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	sh	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. After you apply these styles, you can then create a table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id5876949				0	sh	To Insert a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	sh	Click in your document where you want to create the table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120211.xhp\" name=\"Index/Table\"\>\<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153746				0	sh	Select "Table of Contents" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	sh	Select any options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146872				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896				0	sh	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Additional Styles\</item\> check box in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Create from\</item\> area, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the check box. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Assign Styles\</item\> dialog, click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\> or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\> button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148				0	sh	To Update a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153161				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	sh	Right-click in the table of contents and choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147066				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - All Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text frames from printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	sh	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	sh	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	sh	To Insert a Text Frame				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	sh	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	sh	To Edit a Text Frame				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	sh	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	sh	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	sh	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	sh	To Hide Text From Printing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	sh	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	sh	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	sh	To Link Text Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	sh	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	sh	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	sh	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Frame\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link Frames\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	sh	Click the frame that you want to link to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	sh	You can only link frames if:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	sh	The target frame is empty.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	sh	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	sh	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	sh	The source frame does not have a next link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	sh	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	sh	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	sh	The AutoSize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				20181231 09:50:43
