helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	sh	Place the cursor in the index or table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	sh	If you cannot place your cursor in the index or table of contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</item\>, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Enable\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Cursor in protected areas\</item\> section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	sh	Right-click and choose an editing option from the menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	sh	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
