helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	sh	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	sh	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	sh	To Capitalize Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	sh	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalization in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalizes all letters. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalizes all letters, but in a reduced font size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	sh	To Change Text to Lowercase				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	sh	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	sh	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Adding Bullets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155186				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;turning on and off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; bulleted\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullets;adding and editing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;bullets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;bullets in text documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;bulleting symbols\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155186				0	sh	\<variable id=\"using_numbered_lists\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_numbered_lists.xhp\" name=\"Adding Bullets\"\>Adding Bullets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3291116				0	sh	To Add Bullets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	sh	Select the paragraph(s) that you want to add bullets to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635	16			0	sh	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bullets On/Off\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156108\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_defaultbullet.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156108\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3145403				0	sh	To remove bullets, select the bulleted paragraphs, and then click the \<emph\>Bullets On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154403				0	sh	To Format Bullets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3154416				0	sh	To change the formatting of a bulleted list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	sh	For example, to change the bulleting symbol, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) next to \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Character\</item\>, and then select a special character. You can also click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Graphics\</item\> tab, and then click a symbol style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Selection\</item\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Saving Text Documents in HTML Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>text documents; publishing in HTML\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; creating from text documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>homepage creation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>saving;in HTML format\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	sh	\<variable id=\"send2html\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/send2html.xhp\" name=\"Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\"\>Saving Text Documents in HTML Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149825				0	sh	You can save a $[officename] Writer document in HTML format, so that you can view it in a web browser. If you want, you can associate a page break with a specific heading paragraph style to generate a separate HTML page each time the style appears in the document. $[officename] Writer automatically creates a page containing hyperlinks to each of these pages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	sh	When you save a text document in HTML format, any graphics in the document are saved in JPEG format. The name of the HTML document is added as a prefix to the name of the graphic file. The JPEG images are saved in the same folder as the HTML document and are referenced with <IMG> tags in the HTML code.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3155868				0	sh	Apply one of the default $[officename] heading paragraph styles, for example, "Heading 1", to the paragraphs where you want to generate a new HTML page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3156100				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create HTML Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles\</item\> box, select the paragraph style that you want to use to generate a new HTML page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\send2html.xhp	0	help	par_id3153407				0	sh	Enter a path and a name for the HTML document, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
