helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Defining Borders for Objects 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146957				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>objects; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; for objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; around objects\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>charts;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;borders\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;object borders\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	sh	\<variable id=\"border_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/border_object.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Objects\"\>Defining Borders for Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	sh	In Writer, you can define borders around OLE objects, plug-ins, diagrams/charts, graphics and frames. The name of the menu to be used depends on the object selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673				0	sh	To Set a Predefined Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	sh	Select the object for which you want to define a border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	4			0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	sh	Click one of the predefined border styles. This replaces the current border style of the object with the selected style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152474				0	sh	To Set a Customized Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	sh	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344	9			0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - (object name) – Borders\</item\>.\<br/\>Replace (object name) with the actual name of the object type you selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	sh	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	sh	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3125865				0	sh	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150447				0	sh	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to Contents\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\border_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Using AutoText				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155521				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>AutoText\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>networks and AutoText directories\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;AutoText shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text blocks\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blocks of text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155521				0	sh	\<variable id=\"autotext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/autotext.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoText\"\>Using AutoText\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	sh	In $[officename] Writer, you can store text - also containing graphics, tables, and fields - as AutoText, so that you can quickly insert the text later on. If you want, you can also store formatted text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155539				0	sh	To To Create an AutoText Entry				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155560				0	sh	Select the text, text with graphics, table, or field that you want to save as an AutoText entry. A graphic can only be stored if it is anchored as a character and is preceded and followed by at least one text character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155581				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - AutoText\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147761				0	sh	Select the category where you want to store the AutoText.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147779				0	sh	Type a name that is longer than four characters. This allows you to use the \<emph\>Display remainder of name as suggestion while typing\</emph\> AutoText option. If you want, you can modify the proposed shortcut.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3147807	60			0	sh	Click the \<emph\>AutoText\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_idN10732				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Close\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147282				0	sh	To Insert an AutoText Entry				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145597				0	sh	Click in your document where you want to insert an AutoText entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615				0	sh	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>\<emph\>Edit - AutoText\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145644				0	sh	Select the AutoText that you want to insert, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145668	30			0	sh	You can also type the shortcut for an AutoText entry, and then press F3, or click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoText\</item\> icon on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> bar, and then choose an AutoText entry. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155090	43			0	sh	To quickly enter a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>fn\</item\>, and then press F3. If you insert more than one formula, the formulae are sequentially numbered. To insert dummy text, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>dt\</item\>, and then press F3. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155115				0	sh	To Print a List of AutoText Entries				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155160				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> list, double-click "%PRODUCTNAME Macros - Gimmicks".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277				0	sh	Select "AutoText" and then click \<emph\>Run\</emph\>. A list of the current AutoText entries is generated in a separate text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151304				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151327				0	sh	Using AutoText in Network Installations				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151355				0	sh	You can store AutoText entries in different directories on a network.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370				0	sh	For example, you can store "read-only" AutoText entries for your company on a central server, and user-defined AutoText entries in a local directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	sh	The paths for the AutoText directories can be edited in the configuration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154960				0	sh	Two directories are listed here. The first entry is on the server installation and the second entry is in the user directory. If there are two AutoText entries with the same name in both directories, the entry from the user directory is used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154995				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - AutoText\"\>Edit - AutoText\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\autotext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155012				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\" name=\"Word Completion\"\>Word Completion\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153407				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>page styles; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>blank pages with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>empty page with alternating page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; even/odd pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>title pages; page styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>First Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Left Page page style\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>even/odd pages;formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153407				0	sh	\<variable id=\"even_odd_sdw\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/even_odd_sdw.xhp\" name=\"Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\"\>Alternating Page Styles on Odd and Even Pages\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3154265				0	sh	\<image id=\"img_id3155876\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_designerdialog.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155876\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147126				0	sh	$[officename] can automatically apply alternating page styles on even (left) and odd pages (right) in your document. For example, you can use page styles to display different headers and footers on even and odd pages. The current page style is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\> at the bottom of the workplace.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id8194219				0	sh	To Set Up Alternating Page Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3150526				0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	sh	In the list of page styles, right-click "Left Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3153179				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145267				0	sh	Select "Right Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	sh	In the list of page styles, right-click "Right Page" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	sh	Select "Left Page" in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155561				0	sh	Go to the first page in your document, and double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3155588				0	sh	To add a header to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the header to. In the header frame, type the text that you want to use as the header.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147772				0	sh	To add a footer to one of the page styles, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and choose the page style that you want to add the footer to. In the footer frame, type the text that you want to use as a footer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	sh	If you do not want to have a header or a footer on the title page of your document, apply the "First Page" style to the title page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	sh	To Suppress the Printout of Empty Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	sh	If two even or two odd pages directly follow each other in your document, Writer will insert an empty page by default. You can suppress those automatically generated empty pages from printing and from exporting to PDF.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id8147221				0	sh	Remove the check mark from \<emph\>Print automatically inserted blank pages\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\even_odd_sdw.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04010000.xhp\" name=\"Insert Break dialog\"\>Insert Break dialog\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation/scope\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scope of page styles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	sh	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6418042				0	sh	All page properties for Writer text documents, like for example the page orientation, are defined by page styles. By default, a new text document uses the “Default” page style for all pages. If you open an existing text document, different page styles may have been applied to the different pages. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id8324533				0	sh	It is important to know that changes that you apply to a page property will only affect the pages that use the current page style. The current page style is listed in the Status Bar at the lower window border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	sh	To Change the Page Orientation for All Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6307260				0	sh	If your text document consists only of pages with the same page style, you can change the page properties directly:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	sh	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id4202398				0	sh	To Change the Page Orientation Only for Some Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	sh	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. Page styles define more page properties, as for example header and footer or page margins. You can either change the “Default” page style for the current document, or you can define own page styles and apply those page styles to any parts of your text. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1449324				0	sh	At the end of this help page, we'll discuss the scope of page styles in detail. If you are unsure about the page style concept, please read the section at the end of this page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1480758				0	sh	Unlike character styles or paragraph styles, the page styles don't know a hierarchy. You can create a new page style based on the properties of an existing page style, but when you later change the source style, the new page style does not automatically inherit the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	sh	To change the page orientation for all pages that share the same page style, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	sh	Right-click a page style and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. The new page style initially gets all properties of the selected page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	sh	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	sh	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page that follows a page with the new style. See the section about the scope of page styles at the end of this help page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	sh	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	sh	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	sh	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1658375				0	sh	Now you have defined a proper page style with the name "My Landscape". To apply the new style, double-click the "My Landscape" page style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. All pages in the current scope of page styles will be changed. If you defined the "next style" to be a different style, only the first page of the current scope of page styles will be changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6082949				0	sh	The Scope of Page Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2858668				0	sh	You should be aware of the scope of page styles in %PRODUCTNAME. Which pages of your text document get affected by editing a page style?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3278603				0	sh	One Page Long Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	sh	A page style can be defined to span one page only. The “First Page” style is an example. You set this property by defining another page style to be the "next style", on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	sh	A one page long style starts from the lower border of the current page style range up to the next page break. The next page break appears automatically when the text flows to the next page, which is sometimes called a "soft page break". Alternatively, you can insert a manual page break.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	sh	To insert a manual page break at the cursor position, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> or choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\> and just click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id166020				0	sh	Manually Defined Range of a Page style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	sh	The “Default” page style does not set a different "next style" on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page. Instead, the "next style" is set also to be “Default”. All page styles that are followed by the same page style can span multiple pages. The lower and upper borders of the page style range are defined by "page breaks with style". All the pages between any two "page breaks with style" use the same page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	sh	You can insert a "page break with style" directly at the cursor position. Alternatively, you can apply the "page break with style" property to a paragraph or to a paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6054261				0	sh	Perform any one of the following commands:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1811578				0	sh	To insert a "page break with style" at the cursor position, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\>, select a \<emph\>Style\</emph\> name from the listbox, and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9935911				0	sh	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Text Flow\</item\>. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4753868				0	sh	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph style, right-click the current paragraph. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style\</item\> from the context menu. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4744407				0	sh	To apply the "page break with style" property to an arbitrary paragraph style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>. Click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon. Right-click the name of the paragraph style you want to modify and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Indexes Covering Several Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153418				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;multiple documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>multiple documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;indexes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153418				0	sh	\<variable id=\"indices_multidoc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_multidoc.xhp\" name=\"Indexes Covering Several Documents\"\>Indexes Covering Several Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	sh	There are several ways to create an index that spans several documents:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	sh	Create an \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120210.xhp\" name=\"index in each individual document\"\>index in each individual document\</link\>, copy and paste the indexes into a single document, and then edit them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147118				0	sh	Select each index, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Section\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>\</link\>, and then enter a name for the index. In a separate document, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Section\</item\>, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>), and then locate and insert a named index section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_multidoc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150230				0	sh	Create a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01010001.xhp\" name=\"master document\"\>master document\</link\>, add as subdocuments the files that you want to include in the index, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Inserting an Entire Text Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155185				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>sections;inserting external content\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;merging\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting text documents as\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155185				0	sh	\<variable id=\"textdoc_inframe\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/textdoc_inframe.xhp\" name=\"Inserting an Entire Text Document\"\>Inserting an Entire Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id1812799				0	sh	To Insert a Text File				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	sh	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149839				0	sh	Locate the text document that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3148858				0	sh	The contents of the text document are embedded into the current document and are not updated if the source file is changed. If you want the contents to automatically update when you change the source document, insert the file as a link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	sh	To Insert an Entire Text Document as a Link				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	sh	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	sh	Type a name in the \<emph\>New Section\</emph\> box, and then select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149642				0	sh	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File Name\</item\> box, type the name of the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) and locate the file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968				0	sh	If the target text document contains sections, you can select the section that you want to insert in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sections\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	sh	If you want, set the formatting options for the section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149862				0	sh	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	sh	$[officename] automatically updates the contents of the inserted section whenever the source document is changed. To manually update the contents of the section, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Update All\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156377				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; editing by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard;adding or deleting rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156377				0	sh	\<variable id=\"table_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cells.xhp\" name=\"Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\"\>Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149487				0	sh	You can add or delete rows or columns in tables as well as split or merge table cells using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906				0	sh	To insert a new row in a table, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the up or down arrow key. You can also move the cursor to the last cell in the table, and then press Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	sh	To insert a new column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the left or right arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156096				0	sh	To split a table cell instead of adding a column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you press the left or right arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	sh	To delete a row, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the up or down arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	sh	To delete a column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	sh	To merge a table into an adjacent cell, place the cursor in the cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Resetting Font Attributes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149963				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>formats; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>font attributes; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>fonts; resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resetting; fonts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>direct formatting;exiting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;exiting direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exiting;direct formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149963				0	sh	\<variable id=\"reset_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/reset_format.xhp\" name=\"Resetting Font Attributes\"\>Resetting Font Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154091				0	sh	You can quickly exit manual formatting by pressing the right-arrow key. For example, if you have pressed Ctrl+B to apply the bold typeface to the text that you type, press the right arrow to return to the default character format of the paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\reset_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	sh	To reset all direct formatting of existing text, select that text, then choose the menu command \<emph\>Format - Default Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147407				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; lists, while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;creating while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers;lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic bullets/numbers; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullets; using automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407				0	sh	\<variable id=\"auto_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\"\>Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155525				0	sh	$[officename] can automatically apply numbering or bullets as you type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154243				0	sh	To Enable Automatic Numbering and Bulleting				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152830	29			0	sh	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, and then select “Apply numbering – symbol”.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867				0	sh	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect\</emph\>, and ensure that \<emph\>While Typing\</emph\> is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id2357860				0	sh	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152897				0	sh	To Create a Numbered or Bulleted List While You Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	sh	Type 1., i., or I. to start a numbered list. Type * or - to start a bulleted list. You can also type a right parenthesis after the number instead of a period , for example, 1) or i).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147794				0	sh	Enter a space, type your text, and then press Enter. The new paragraph automatically receives the next number or bullet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147814				0	sh	Press Enter again to finish the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	sh	You can start a numbered list with any number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154083				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Numbering/Bullets\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
