helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149482				0	sh	Language				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151252				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_DLG_SORTING_LB_LANG\"\>Select the language that defines the sorting rules.\</ahelp\> Some languages sort special characters differently than other languages.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149104				0	sh	Match case				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154838				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_DLG_SORTING_CB_CASE\"\>Distinguishes between uppercase and lowercase letters when you sort a table. For Asian languages special handling applies.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10895				0	sh	For Asian languages, select \<emph\>Match case \</emph\>to apply multi-level collation. In the multi-level collation, the primitive forms of the entries are first compared with the cases of the forms and diacritics ignored. If the forms are the same, the diacritics of the forms are compared. If the forms are still the same, the cases, character widths, and Japanese Kana differences of the forms are compared.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Editing Tables Using the Keyboard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154506				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>tables; editing with the keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154506				0	sh	\<variable id=\"tabelle_tastatur\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05090201.xhp\" name=\"Editing Tables Using the Keyboard\"\>Editing Tables Using the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145244				0	sh	You can resize and delete table columns with the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150564				0	sh	Resizing Columns and Rows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153920				0	sh	To resize a column, place the cursor in a table cell, hold down Alt, and then press the left or the right arrow. To resize the column without changing the width of the table, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147566				0	sh	To increase the left indent of the table, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift, and then press the right arrow.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150759				0	sh	To resize a row, place the cursor in the row, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the up or the down arrows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149286				0	sh	To move the table downwards on the page, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift, and then press the down arrow.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151176				0	sh	Inserting and deleting columns or rows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147512				0	sh	To insert a column, place the cursor in a table cell, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and press Insert, release, and then press the left or the right arrow.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940				0	sh	To delete a column, place the cursor in the column that you want to delete, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and press Delete, release, and then press the left or the right arrow.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154105				0	sh	To insert a row, place the cursor in a table cell, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and press Insert, release, and then press the up or the down arrow.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153531				0	sh	To delete a row, place the cursor in the row that you want to delete, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and press Delete, release, and then press the up or the down arrow.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150983				0	sh	To change the behavior of tables in a text document, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040500.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Table\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</link\>\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05090201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154196				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/main0204.xhp\" name=\"Table Bar\"\>Table Bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Variables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	bm_id8526261				0	sh	\<bookmark_value\>user-defined fields, restriction\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153716				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>Variables\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764				0	sh	Variable fields let you add dynamic content to your document. For example, you can use a variable to reset the page numbering.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149759				0	sh	User-defined fields are only available in the current document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243625				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	sh	Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	sh	Description				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149803				0	sh	Set Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150996				0	sh	Defines a variable and its value. You can change the value of a variable by clicking in front of the variable field, and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Field\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	sh	Show Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669	9			0	sh	Inserts the current value of the variable that you click in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147531				0	sh	DDE field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	sh	Inserts a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link into the document, that you can update as often as you want through the assigned name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	sh	Insert Formula				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	sh	Inserts a fixed number, or the result of a formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149494				0	sh	Input field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	sh	Inserts a new value for a variable or a User Field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098				0	sh	The value of a variable in an Input field is only valid from where the field is inserted and onwards. To change the value of the variable later in the document, insert another Input field of the same name, but with a different value. However, the value of a User Field is changed globally.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	sh	The variables are displayed in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> field. When you click the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> button, the dialog\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"Input Field\"\>\<emph\>Input Field\</emph\>\</link\> appears, where you can enter the new value or additional text as a remark.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149034				0	sh	Number range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	sh	Inserts automatic numbering for tables, graphics, or text frames.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	sh	Set page variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	sh	Inserts a reference point in the document, after which the page count restarts. Select "on" to enable the reference point, and "off" to disable it. You can also enter an offset to start the page count at a different number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156267				0	sh	Show Page Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588				0	sh	Displays the number of pages from the "Set page variable" reference point to this field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	sh	User Field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151377				0	sh	Inserts a custom global variable. You can use the User Field to define a variable for a condition statement. When you change a User Field, all instances of the variable in the document are updated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243892				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3148886	25			0	sh	For user-defined fields, click the format that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243880				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Type the name of the user-defined field that you want to create.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243951				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the contents that you want to add to a user-defined field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_LISTBOX_TP_FLD_VAR_LB_VARFORMAT\"\>In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, define if the value is inserted as text or a number.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3888363				0	sh	Selection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id7453535				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:TP_FLD_DOK:LB_DOKSELECTION\"\>Lists the available fields for the field type selected in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list. To insert a field, click the field, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3326822				0	sh	To quickly insert a field from the list, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and double-click the field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150696	36			0	sh	In an HTML document, two additional fields are available for the "Set variable" field type: HTML_ON and HTML_OFF. The text that you type in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box is converted to an opening HTML \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tag\"\>tag\</link\> (<Value>) or to a closing HTML (</Value>) tag when the file is saved as an HTML document, depending on the option that you select.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149555				0	sh	If you double-click an entry while holding the Ctrl key or select the desired variable and press the spacebar, it is immediately inserted into your document.				20181231 09:50:43
