helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154106				0	sh	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090007.xhp\" name=\"Special Tags\"\>Special Tags\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669				0	sh	When you save a document that contains fields as an HTML document, $[officename] automatically converts date, time, and DocInformation fields to special HTML tags. The field contents are inserted between the opening and closing HTML tags of the converted fields. These special HTML tags do not correspond to standard HTML tags.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	sh	$[officename] Writer fields are identified by the <SDFIELD> tag in an HTML document. The field type, the format, and the name of the special field are included in the opening HTML tag. The format of a field tag that is recognized by an HTML filter depends on the field type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154570				0	sh	Date and Time Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149696				0	sh	For "Date" and "Time" fields, the TYPE parameter equals DATETIME. The format of the date or the time is specified by the SDNUM parameter, for example, DD:MM:YY for dates, or HH:MM:SS for time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155183				0	sh	For fixed date and time fields, the date or the time is specified by the SDVAL parameter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149485				0	sh	Examples of date and time special HTML tags that are recognized by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3151257				0	sh	Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3148970				0	sh	$[officename] Tag				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147102				0	sh	Date is fixed				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634				0	sh	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4239988426" SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155137				0	sh	Date is variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3156275				0	sh	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;DD/MM/YY">17/02/98</SDFIELD>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3145774				0	sh	Time is fixed				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	sh	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDVAL="35843,4240335648" SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3150110				0	sh	Time is variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3155862				0	sh	<SDFIELD TYPE=DATETIME SDNUM="1031;1031;HH:MM:SS">10:10:36</SDFIELD>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147409				0	sh	DocInformation Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147487				0	sh	For DocInformation fields, the TYPE parameter equals DOCINFO. The SUBTYPE parameter displays the specific field type, for example, for the "Created" DocInformation field, SUBTYPE=CREATE. For date and time DocInformation fields, the FORMAT parameter equals DATE or TIME, and the SDNUM parameter indicates the number format that is used. The SDFIXED parameter indicates if the content of the DocInformation field is fixed or not.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3147501				0	sh	The contents of a fixed date or time field are equal to the SDVAL parameter, otherwise the contents are equal to the text found between the SDFIELD HTML tags.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090007.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	sh	Examples of DocInformation special HTML tags that are recognized by $[officename] as fields are shown in the following table:				20181231 09:50:43
