helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3149096				0	sh	Use this area to specify which information to include in an index.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149815				0	sh	Outline				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3151253				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_FROMHEADINGS\"\>Creates the index using outline levels, that is, paragraphs formatted with one of the predefined heading styles (Heading 1-10) are added to the index.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id1209200804373840				0	sh	You can also assign the outline levels in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\"\>Outline & Numbering\</link\> tab page of the Format - Paragraph dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153633				0	sh	Additional Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	sh	\<variable id=\"vorlg\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_ADDSTYLES\"\>Includes the paragraph styles that you specify in the \<emph\>Assign Styles\</emph\> dialog as index entries. To select the paragraph styles that you want to include in the index, click the \<emph\>Assign Styles (...\</emph\>) button to the right of this box.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149168				0	sh	...				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3145776				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_SELECT:PB_ADDSTYLES\"\>Opens the \<emph\>Assign Styles\</emph\> dialog, where you can select the paragraph styles to include in the index.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151374				0	sh	Index marks				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	sh	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_TOX_SELECT:CB_TOXMARKS\"\>Includes the index entries that you inserted by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\> in the index.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sh	Hyphenation				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154657				0	sh	Hyphenation				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148572				0	sh	\<variable id=\"silben\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts hyphens in words that are too long to fit at the end of a line.\</ahelp\> $[officename] searches the document and suggests hyphenation that you can accept or reject. If text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the selected text only. If no text is selected, the Hyphenation dialog works on the whole document.\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153811				0	sh	To automatically hyphenate the current or selected paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\> tab. You can also apply automatic hyphenation to a paragraph style. In text where automatic hyphenation is enabled, the Hyphenation dialog will not find any word to hyphenate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	sh	When $[officename] finds a word that requires hyphenation, do one of the following options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622				0	sh	To accept the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558				0	sh	To change the hyphenation of the displayed word, click the left or right arrow below the word, and then click \<emph\>Hyphenate\</emph\>. The left and right buttons are enabled for words with multiple hyphenation points.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150017				0	sh	To reject the hyphenation of the displayed word, click \<emph\>Skip\</emph\>. This word will not be hyphenated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	sh	To automatically hyphenate the remaining part of the selection or the document, click \<emph\>Hyphenate All\</emph\> and answer "Yes" to the following question.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150019				0	sh	To end hyphenation, click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>. The hyphenation that is applied already will not be reverted. You can use \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\> to undo all hyphenation that was applied while the Hyphenation dialog was open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147562				0	sh	To exclude paragraphs from the automatic hyphenation, select the paragraphs, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>, click the Text Flow tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box in the Hyphenation area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154276				0	sh	To disable the Hyphenation dialog and always hyphenate automatically, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010400.xhp\" name=\"Language Settings - Writing Aids\"\>Language Settings - Writing Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and select the \<emph\>Hyphenate without inquiry\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	sh	To manually enter a hyphen directly in the document, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign (-).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147523				0	sh	To insert a non-breaking (protected) hyphen directly in the document, click in the word that you want to hyphenate, and then press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Minus sign(-).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573				0	sh	To hide custom hyphens, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040600.xhp\" name=\"Text Document - Formatting Aids\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</link\>\</emph\>, and then clear the \<emph\>Custom hyphens\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150360				0	sh	Word				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06030000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153676				0	sh	Word				20181231 09:50:43
